# =========================================================================
#  DEVELOPER NOTES - KNOWN PITFALLS & PREVIOUSLY FIXED BUGS
# =========================================================================
#  DO NOT repeat these mistakes. If you're editing related code, check here first.
#
#  1. SHIELD BATTERY ABILITY: The shield battery recharge ability is
#     AbilityId.SHIELDBATTERYRECHARGEEX5_SHIELDBATTERYRECHARGE.
#     NEVER use AbilityId.DUMMYABIL298_DUMMYABIL298 -- it does NOT exist
#     in the AbilityId enum and will crash with AttributeError.
#
#  2. BUILDER PROBE MANAGEMENT: When the builder probe finishes a task,
#     you MUST clear builder_probe_tag, builder_locked, builder_current_task,
#     and builder_task_target. Missing any of these causes the builder to
#     stand idle at the build site forever.
#
#  3. STATE MACHINE TRANSITIONS: After emergency defense (hatch_first_lings_spotted),
#     the wall_step must be normalized back to the standard path. The
#     _emergency_to_standard_done flag gates the transition. If this flag
#     is never set, the build order stalls permanently after defense.
#
#  4. TWILIGHT COUNCIL BUILD: The twilight council requires vespene >= 100
#     AND (sentry exists OR already_pending). In the emergency defense path,
#     we may have no sentry, so the emergency_no_sentry bypass must be checked.
#     Without this bypass, twilight never builds after emergency defense.
#
#  5. ALREADY_PENDING CHECKS: When gating unit production on "unit exists",
#     always check BOTH self.units(TYPE).amount AND self.already_pending(TYPE).
#     Checking only one causes the sequence to fire twice (once while building,
#     once after completion) or not at all.
#
#  6. HATCH-FIRST BUILD ORDER (PvZ, no lings): After cyber core completes,
#     the unit order is: Zealot > Sentry > Adept x4 > Stalkers (until charge)
#     > Zealots (after charge). We ONLY switch to stalkers before charge when
#     a roach warren is scouted (handled by _roach_defense_active, which
#     deactivates _hatch_first_active entirely). The sentry is trained in
#     State 67, adepts in State 67.5. The zealot is trained by
#     manage_army_production SEQUENCE 1 (before cyber is ready).
#     DO NOT change to adept-first -- the sentry provides guardian shield
#     for the army push and force fields for defensive holds.
#     DEV NOTE #151: Before charge, _hatch_first_active Step 2 produces
#     adepts up to 4, then stalkers. Roach warren detection switches to
#     pure stalkers via _roach_defense_active.
#
#  7. SUPPLY BLOCK PREVENTION: Pylons must continue being built above 150
#     supply. The supply check must not have an upper bound that stops
#     pylon production. Check manage_supply for the supply_cap logic.
#
#  8. ZEALOTS VS FLYING STRUCTURES: Zealots and sentries CANNOT attack
#     flying structures (lifted Terran buildings). In the army sweep code,
#     ground-only melee units must be filtered out when the only remaining
#     targets are flying. Stalkers/voidrays handle flying cleanup.
#
#  9. STATE MACHINE VS GENERAL PRODUCTION RACE: When a state machine state
#     (e.g. State 67) is responsible for training a unit (e.g. sentry),
#     the general production sequences (SEQUENCE 2, 3, 4 in
#     manage_army_production) MUST be suppressed for that unit. Otherwise
#     SEQUENCE 2 trains the sentry first, making the state machine's
#     condition permanently false, stalling the build order forever.
#     ALWAYS add a skip condition in the general production sequences when
#     the state machine controls that unit's training order.
#
#  10. UPGRADE ID NAMES: The correct UpgradeId for blink is BLINKTECH.
#      NEVER use BLINKTECHRESEARCH -- it does NOT exist in UpgradeId and
#      will crash with AttributeError. Same class of bug as DUMMYABIL298.
#
#  11. BUILDER STUCK COUNTER VS MINERAL WAIT: When the builder is idle at
#      the pylon target, do NOT increment the stuck counter if the builder
#      can't afford the pylon. Warpgate production drains minerals every
#      frame, so the builder may wait 10+ frames for minerals. If the stuck
#      counter increments during this wait, it exhausts, blacklists the
#      position, and eventually ALL positions are blacklisted. This cascade
#      causes the bot to stop building pylons entirely (supply cap stuck).
#      DEV NOTE #166: Same pattern applies to forge — don't count idle
#      retries when can't afford forge. The builder is waiting for minerals,
#      not stuck at an invalid position.
#
#  11b. BUILDER TASK MUST BE SET BEFORE MOVE (NOT JUST BUILD): When a state
#      machine issues builder.move(target) to walk the probe to a build
#      position, it MUST also set builder_current_task and builder_task_target
#      at the same time. Previously, nf_state 70.5 only set these when
#      builder.build() was called (after arrival), leaving builder_current_task
#      = None during the walk phase. This allowed manage_production_buildings()
#      to find a DIFFERENT twilight position and assign it, creating a bounce:
#      nf_state issues move to position A, SUPPLY system sets task to position B,
#      is_builder_busy re-issues move to B, nf_state re-issues move to A, repeat
#      forever — twilight never gets built. The fix: set builder_current_task
#      and builder_task_target immediately when issuing the move command, so the
#      SUPPLY system's guard (not builder_current_task == "twilight") blocks it.
#
#  12. STALKER DEFENDER TAG FLIP BUG: In _proxy_hidden_tech_stalker_micro,
#      the reaper defender assignment MUST NOT be reassigned every frame based
#      on which stalker is closest to ourmain. The old logic caused two
#      stalkers to swap the defender tag every frame: Stalker A gets assigned
#      defender and moved to cybercore; Stalker B chases reaper toward
#      ourmain; B is now closer to ourmain and gets reassigned as defender,
#      pulled back to cybercore; A is released, starts chasing reaper toward
#      ourmain; A becomes closest again, gets reassigned defender... Both
#      stalkers bounce between cybercore and the reaper direction every frame,
#      neither ever attacks. FIX: Defender assignment is STABLE -- only
#      changes on death or reaper threat disappearing. With <5 stalkers,
#      ALL stalkers chase the reaper (no dedicated defender at cybercore).
#
#  13. STALKER move() vs attack(): When chasing enemies, use attack()
#      (attack-move) NOT move(). move() causes the stalker to walk past
#      enemies without shooting. attack() auto-engages when in range.
#      This applies everywhere in the wall defense priority logic.
#
#  14. PVP STALKER BATTERY RETREAT + NATURAL LEASH: The old battery
#      leash radius (6, then 10 from battery) caused problems: stalkers
#      were anchored to battery instead of defending workers/structures,
#      and the <50% retreat threshold meant stalkers died before
#      retreating. FIX: Replaced battery leash with a NATURAL BASE leash
#      (25 from ournat). When HP < 80%, stalkers kite-retreat toward the
#      nearest shield battery: on weapon cooldown, move toward battery;
#      off cooldown, attack ONLY if an enemy is within weapon range of
#      the retreating stalker. When HP >= 80% and within natural leash,
#      stalkers fight freely (zonal > adept > standard). If a stalker
#      goes beyond 25 from ournat, it attack-moves toward battery (it
#      shoots on the way back). The battery is the retreat TARGET, but
#      the natural is the leash BOUNDARY -- there is no leash radius on
#      the battery itself.
#
#  15. PVP ZONAL DEFENSE: Oracles/air units can fly into our main or
#      natural and kill workers while our stalkers sit anchored to the
#      shield battery. The battery-centric defense only detected enemies
#      within 20 of the battery, missing threats at our main base (~29
#      away from battery). FIX: Added zonal defense layer that detects
#      ANY enemy within 25 of ourmain OR 25 of ournat as highest
#      priority. Stalkers at >= 80% HP attack freely in zonal range.
#      Stalkers at < 80% HP kite-retreat toward battery (shoot off
#      cooldown if enemy in range, retreat on cooldown). Sentries,
#      voidrays, and zealots always respond to zonal threats.
#
#  16. MANAGE_SUPPLY_MIDGAME VS 4-GATE STATE MACHINE: self.build() uses
#      the SC2 framework's worker selection, which does NOT respect our
#      custom builder_probe_tag lock. When the 4-gate state machine is
#      building the main pylon (state 5-5.5), manage_supply_midgame must
#      NOT call self.build(PYLON) -- it will steal the builder probe,
#      cancel the main pylon order, and place the pylon at the natural
#      instead. FIX: Skip supply building when proxy hidden tech / proxy
#      rax is active and four_gate_state <= 5.5.
#
#  17. GATEWAY SEARCH RADIUS IN GATEWAY_FIRST: In execute_pvt_gateway_first,
#      the gateway is built at gatewall1 (the wall position), which is
#      typically 25-35 units from ourmain. NEVER use closer_than(10, ourmain)
#      to find the gateway -- it will miss it entirely, causing the state
#      machine to permanently stall at step 4 (never finds gateway, never
#      builds cyber core, never transitions to 4-gate). ALWAYS search near
#      gatewall1 instead, with a fallback to all gateways. This applies to
#      both the state 4 gateway progress check AND the parallel pre-move
#      during gas states (2, 2.5, 3, 3.5).
#
#  18. CHASE PROBE SELF-REFERENTIAL LOCK: is_worker_locked() includes
#      _pvp_suspicious_chaser_tag and _pvp_chase_probe_tags in its checks.
#      This means a chase probe is ALWAYS detected as "locked" by its own
#      assignment. When _pvp_early_probe_detect or _pvp_cannon_rush_chase_probes
#      checks is_worker_locked() to see if a chase probe was "stolen" by
#      the builder system, it sees the probe as locked (by its own chase
#      assignment) and releases it. Next frame, a new chaser is assigned,
#      same thing happens. This causes the chaser to flip every frame --
#      no probe ever actually chases. FIX: Before calling is_worker_locked()
#      on a chase probe, temporarily clear _pvp_suspicious_chaser_tag and
#      _pvp_chase_probe_tags so the probe's own assignment doesn't make it
#      appear locked. Also add _pvp_suspicious_chaser_tag and
#      _pvp_chase_probe_tags to get_free_worker's exclusion list so the
#      builder doesn't steal chase probes.
#
#  19. CANNON RUSH: NO PROBE CHASE AFTER CANNONS COMPLETE: Once enemy
#      photon cannons are completed (ready), our probes must NOT be sent
#      to chase enemy probes or attack cannons near our base. Completed
#      cannons will kill our probes in 2-3 shots. Probes should ONLY be
#      pulled to chase during the build window (cannons under construction)
#      -- that's when probe attacks can deny the cannon. After cannons
#      are up, only military units (zealots, stalkers) should engage.
#
#  20. BUILDER PROBE REPLACE (NOT RELEASE) ON LOW HP: When the builder
#      probe drops below 40% HP from worker harass, do NOT just release
#      it back to mining -- it will die. Instead, IMMEDIATELY replace it
#      with a fresh full-health probe using get_free_worker(prefer_full_health).
#      Transfer the builder state (probe_tag, locked, task, target) to the
#      replacement so the build continues seamlessly. The old probe is sent
#      to mine minerals. If no replacement is available, then fall back to
#      releasing builder state. Also: when transferring probe tags between
#      state machines (e.g., gw_first → reaper_response), ALWAYS verify the
#      probe is alive with self.workers.find_by_tag() first -- a dead probe
#      tag will cause infinite "Transferring..." spam every frame.
#
#  21. PVT ZONAL DEFENSE = 25 FROM OURMAIN ALWAYS: The PvT stalker defense
#      must ALWAYS use 25 from ourmain as the threat zone, not 15. A
#      battlecruiser can warp into the main base while stalkers sit at the
#      natural -- 15 from ourmain is too short to detect and respond. This
#      is the same 25-from-main/25-from-nat zonal defense used in PvP.
#      The old code only expanded to 25 when _pvt_air_threat_detected was
#      True (starport+techlab scouted), but BC rushes don't always have
#      a starport detected early enough.
#
#  22. PVZ HATCH-FIRST RALLY TO OURNAT: Gateway rally points in the
#      hatch-first no-lings path must rally to ournat, NOT to the
#      cybercore/gw2 gap. The gap rally caused units to spawn OUTSIDE
#      the wall where they get picked off by zerglings. Rallying to
#      ournat ensures units spawn inside the wall where shield batteries
#      can support them.
#
#  23. PVZ BUILD ORDER: MAIN PYLON BEFORE NAT SHIELD BATTERY: In the
#      hatch-first no-lings path, the build order was:
#        3rd shield battery → nat shield battery → forge → main pylon → twilight
#      This delayed the main pylon (which twilight needs for power), causing
#      charge to finish too late against the roach-ravager timing attack.
#      New order:
#        3rd shield battery → main pylon → nat shield battery → forge → twilight
#      This ensures the main pylon exists early, so twilight starts sooner
#      and charge completes in time. State transitions changed:
#        67.6→67.7 (was 67.65), 67.8→67.65 (was 70), 67.67→70 (was 67.7)
#      All rebuild states (67.85/67.86) also transition to 67.65 instead of 70.
#      Lings-spotted skips in 67.65/67.67 go to 70 (twilight) not 67.7.
#
#  24. PVZ DON'T WAIT FOR 2ND ADEPT BEFORE 3RD SHIELD BATTERY: State 67.5
#      used to block until 2 adepts were trained before transitioning to the
#      3rd shield battery state. This delayed the entire build order. Now
#      state 67.5 transitions as soon as the 3rd pylon is complete, regardless
#      of adept count. The 2nd adept is trained by manage_army_production's
#      new hatch-first adept sequence. If roach warren is spotted, stalkers
#      are produced instead of the 2nd adept. This further ensures twilight
#      comes out on time for charge vs roach-rav timing.
#
#  25. PVT REAPER INTERCEPT: ONLY 1 STALKER CHASES REAPER: When a reaper
#      enters our main base while cyclones are attacking our wall/nat, ALL
#      stalkers should NOT divert to chase the reaper. Only 1 stalker should
#      be assigned as the reaper interceptor with intercept micro (pincer
#      positioning between reaper and mineral center). The rest zonally
#      defend and attack the nearest enemy unit to them (cyclones, marines,
#      etc.). If the reaper is the ONLY enemy near our base, then all
#      stalkers chase it. This applies to both _proxy_hidden_tech_stalker_micro
#      (post-sweep defender now actively chases reaper instead of holding at
#      cybercore) and manage_pvt_stalker_defense (reaper intercept tag
#      assignment when threats_main contains a reaper alongside other threats).
#      The interceptor is STABLE -- only changes on death or reaper threat
#      disappearing (same anti-flip logic as note #12).
#
#  26. 4-GATE STATE 5→5.5 TRANSITION: DO NOT CLEAR pylon_ordered! When the
#      main pylon is ordered in state 5 and we transition to 5.5 (supply
#      pylon), pylon_ordered must remain True until the main pylon actually
#      appears in structures (pylon_count >= 2). The old code cleared
#      pylon_ordered on transition, which caused state 5.5 to immediately
#      try building a supply pylon. Since the builder probe was still en
#      route to the main pylon position, the supply pylon build order
#      overrode the main pylon move order, sending the probe to the wrong
#      location and cancelling the main pylon. The main pylon never got
#      built, and the bot was stuck with only 1-2 pylons all game. FIX:
#      Set _4gate_main_pylon_in_transit flag on transition. State 5.5
#      checks this flag and returns early (no build orders) until the main
#      pylon appears in structures. Only then does it clear the flag and
#      proceed with the supply pylon.
#
#  27. ADEPT SHADE TO 3RD: ALL ADEPTS, NOT JUST FIRST BATCH:
#      _dispatch_adept_shade_to_3rd() sets _adept_shade_3rd_dispatched=True
#      after the FIRST batch of adepts shades. If only 1 adept existed when
#      the function ran, subsequent adepts (2nd, 3rd, etc.) are NEVER shaded
#      because: (a) _dispatch_adept_shade_to_3rd() returns immediately when
#      _adept_shade_3rd_dispatched=True, and (b) _manage_adept_no_lings()
#      Phase 5 skips adepts > 8 from the 3rd target with "continue".
#      FIX: In _manage_adept_no_lings(), add a check for adepts that are
#      > 5 from the 3rd gap position when there are no threats (no lings
#      near wall, no lings near 3rd, not retreating). Shade those adepts
#      to the 3rd gap. This runs per-frame so new adepts automatically
#      get shaded. Skip adepts already casting shade.
#
#  28. WARPGATE PRODUCTION STALL: TWO ROOT CAUSES:
#      (a) SEQUENCE 4 (main production) requires a COMPLETED Twilight Council
#          via self.structures(UnitTypeId.TWILIGHTCOUNCIL). While twilight is
#          under construction (already_pending but not yet complete), SEQUENCE 4
#          can't fire. After adept(2) + sentry(1) + stalker(1) are done, ALL
#          the elif conditions are False → production falls through with NOTHING
#          being warped in. FIX: Also accept already_pending(TWILIGHTCOUNCIL)
#          in the SEQUENCE 4 guard condition.
#      (b) can_place() with random offset has no fallback: when the random
#          offset puts the position outside the power field or on blocked
#          terrain, can_place returns False and the warpgate stays IDLE that
#          frame. No find_placement() fallback exists. Over many frames this
#          can cause long stalls. FIX: Use find_placement() as fallback when
#          can_place fails, and when 3rd pylon exists in PvZ, warp in around
#          the 3rd pylon instead of the natural wall pylon (more space).
#
#  29. PVT SIEGE TANK DEFENSE + BUILD STALL: THREE ISSUES:
#      (a) _proxy_hidden_tech_stalker_micro chase limit was 20 from base.
#          Siege tanks siege up at 25-30 from ournat — outside the 20 limit.
#          Stalkers hold position at the wall instead of running the tank down.
#          FIX: Increased chase limit to 30 (35 for siege tanks specifically).
#          Also increased manage_pvt_stalker_defense _nat_threat_range minimum
#          from 20 to 30 so siege tanks are detected as zonal threats.
#      (b) manage_pvt_stalker_defense _nat_threat_range was only 20 when air
#          threat was active. A siege tank at 25 from ournat was invisible to
#          the zonal defense system. FIX: _nat_threat_range = max(30, nat_defense_range)
#          — never less than 30, regardless of air threat mode.
#      (c) gw_first state machine stuck at state 2 after 4-gate chain built gas.
#          The 4-gate state machine builds gas at t=60-63s, but the gw_first
#          state machine (which runs every frame separately) was at state 2
#          ("build gas 1"). After t=60s, it tried to find a free worker to
#          build gas, but all workers were already on gas or fighting —
#          get_free_worker() returned None, causing the state to never advance.
#          Since the state machine never reached state 6 (done), manage_supply
#          and other systems that depend on it being complete may not function
#          correctly. FIX: Added safety check at state 2 and 3 — if both gases
#          already exist as structures, skip directly to state 4 (cyber pre-move).
#
#  30. PVT WALL GAP HOLD + NAT_LEASH: TWO ISSUES causing stalkers to hold
#      position at wall instead of pushing out to fight ranged Terran units:
#      (a) Wall gap hold_position (manage_army_movement A3) was applied to ALL
#          matchups including PvT. This code issues hold_position to any unit
#          within 1 of the wall gap, preventing them from receiving attack
#          orders. It's designed for PvP/PvZ where melee units (zealots,
#          zerglings) can flood through the gap — but Terran has NO melee
#          flood. In PvT, this hold_position overrides attack commands from
#          manage_pvt_stalker_defense every frame, causing massive attack
#          resets (145 resets / 263 attacks = 55% reset rate observed).
#          FIX: Skip wall gap hold_position entirely for PvT (not self.vs_terran).
#          Also clear _enemy_near_wallgap flag for PvT since no melee traversal
#          blocking is needed.
#      (b) NAT_LEASH = 25 in _proxy_hidden_tech_stalker_micro shield battery
#          retreat section was too restrictive. Siege tanks siege up at 25-30
#          from ournat. Stalkers chasing them are at ~27-30 from ournat, which
#          exceeds NAT_LEASH of 25, causing the battery retreat to pull them
#          back before they can engage. The attack → retreat → attack cycle
#          causes attack resets every 2 frames. FIX: Increased NAT_LEASH from
#          25 to 30, matching the chase range increase from Note #29. Stalkers
#          can now push out to engage siege tanks at the edge of the zonal
#          defense zone while still being prevented from deep overextension.
#
#  31. PVT SWEEP CANCELLED BY BATTERY RETREAT: When the 5-stalker sweep is
#      active and stalkers are at the enemy base (100+ from ournat), the
#      shield battery retreat section in _proxy_hidden_tech_stalker_micro
#      pulls ALL stalkers back every frame because they exceed NAT_LEASH.
#      Even with NAT_LEASH=30, sweep stalkers at the enemy base are way
#      beyond that range. A single reaper appearing at our base causes
#      all stalkers to turn around and walk home — the push is completely
#      abandoned. The reaper defender assignment (1 stalker) exists but is
#      irrelevant because the battery retreat runs FIRST and gives all
#      stalkers retreat orders before the reaper defender logic can run.
#      FIX: Skip both NAT_LEASH pull-back AND HP-based battery retreat
#      when the sweep is active (_sweep_active_br flag). During sweep,
#      the sweep's own micro handles kiting (cyclone flee, close enemy
#      kiting, depot focus-fire). The reaper defender handles reapers at
#      base. Only pre-sweep stalkers (<5) should be leashed to battery.
#
#  32. PVT PROXY HIDDEN TECH SWEEP CANCELLED BY manage_army_movement:
#      When the 5-stalker sweep is active in _proxy_hidden_tech_stalker_micro,
#      stalkers are at the enemy base pushing. A single reaper appearing in
#      our base causes ALL stalkers to turn around and walk home, completely
#      abandoning the push. The root cause is that manage_army_movement()
#      runs AFTER manage_pvt_stalker_defense() in on_step and does NOT
#      exclude proxy hidden tech from its base defense and army positioning
#      logic. The two exclusion checks (pvt_stalker_defense_active at the
#      base defense section, and the early return at the army positioning
#      section) included _pvt_proxy_rax but NOT _pvt_proxy_hidden_tech.
#      This means manage_army_movement() finds the reaper near our base,
#      gives ALL stalkers attack orders against it (overriding sweep micro),
#      then repositions them to main_army_pos. The reaper defender in
#      _proxy_hidden_tech_stalker_micro is irrelevant because
#      manage_army_movement() runs after it and overrides the sweep orders
#      with base defense orders. FIX: Added _pvt_proxy_hidden_tech to both
#      exclusion checks, same as _pvt_proxy_rax. Now manage_army_movement()
#      skips stalker base defense AND army positioning for proxy hidden tech,
#      letting _proxy_hidden_tech_stalker_micro handle everything via the
#      dedicated reaper defender (1 stalker) and sweep micro (rest push).
#
#  33. PVT VISION-LOSS CHASE: When stalkers are defending (pre-sweep, <5
#      stalkers) and chasing an enemy unit like a reaper, if the target
#      goes out of vision (e.g., reaper jumps a cliff, enters fog of war),
#      the stalker's attack order persists and it walks toward the last
#      known position indefinitely — chasing nothing across the map. The
#      wall defense section in _proxy_hidden_tech_stalker_micro skipped
#      stalkers with existing ATTACK orders without checking if the target
#      was still visible. FIX: Added a vision check before the "skip
#      stalkers already fighting" logic. If the attack target is a unit
#      tag (int) and self.enemy_units.find_by_tag() returns None (target
#      went out of vision), recall the stalker to wall_rally (cybercore).
#      This only applies when the sweep is NOT active (pre-sweep defense
#      phase) — during sweep, stalkers should keep pushing regardless.
#
#  34. PVT SWEEP DISTRACTED BY PROXY STRUCTURES NEAR OUR BASE: During
#      the 5-stalker sweep, stalkers would attack enemy structures (barracks,
#      factory, etc.) within 50 of ourmain instead of pushing to the enemy
#      base. The proxy rax sweep micro (Priority 6) targeted any structure
#      within 15 of the stalker, and the proxy hidden tech sweep micro
#      (Priority 4) targeted any structure within 20 of the stalker.
#      Neither filtered out structures near our base. Additionally, on
#      weapon cooldown, stalkers near our base would kite from close enemies
#      instead of moving toward the enemy base, getting stuck in a loop of
#      attacking and kiting around proxy structures. FIX: Three changes:
#      (a) Both structure targeting sections now filter out structures
#      within 50 of ourmain -- these are proxy structures near home that
#      distract the sweep. (b) On weapon cooldown, if the stalker is
#      within 50 of ourmain, it moves toward enemymain instead of kiting
#      locally. This ensures sweep stalkers push through our base area
#      toward the enemy instead of getting stuck fighting proxy buildings.
#
#  35. PVZ DEFENSE RECALL: When our army is out attacking in PvZ and the
#      enemy counter-attacks with overwhelming force in our base, we didn't
#      pull our units back to defend. The existing PvZ defense mode only
#      activates when the army is NOT committed (lead unit within 70 of
#      enemymain). If the army is already deep in enemy territory, the
#      defense mode never triggers, and our base gets destroyed while the
#      army keeps attacking enemy buildings. FIX: Added a new defense
#      recall system specifically for when wall structures are destroyed.
#      When enemy combat units are closer_than 50 to ourmain AND our wall
#      structures (gw3 gateway, forge at gatewall3, cannon1) are all
#      destroyed, the army is recalled to defend. The army attack-moves
#      to the enemy unit closest_to ourmain and stays defending until
#      enemy unit count near ourmain is less than our unit count near
#      ourmain. Then we clean up remaining enemies around our base before
#      resuming the attack push. The "wall destroyed" condition is key:
#      while the wall is intact, the cannon and wall pathing provide
#      defense. But once those structures are gone, our base is completely
#      open and workers are defenseless -- that's when we MUST pull back.
#
#  36. PVZ ROACH DEFENSE ZEALOT FALLBACK: In the roach/bane defense
#      production code, step 4 builds a zealot as a fallback when we
#      can't afford a stalker. But when a roach warren is spotted,
#      zealots are terrible against roaches -- they're melee and get
#      kited to death by ranged roach fire. Building zealots wastes
#      gateway time and minerals on units that can't fight roaches
#      effectively. In the match log, after zealot > sentry > 1 stalker,
#      the bot produced 2 more zealots instead of stalkers because it
#      couldn't afford stalkers (gas-limited) and fell through to the
#      zealot fallback. Against 5+ roaches, 2 zealots do nothing while
#      2 stalkers could kite and deal damage. FIX: When a roach warren
#      has been spotted (_pvz_roach_warren_seen), skip the zealot
#      fallback entirely and wait for stalkers. The zealot fallback
#      is still useful for bane-only aggression (no roach warren) where
#      zealots can tank bane hits and deal damage.
#
#  55b. WALL GAP PLUG ZEALOT HOLD POSITION TIMING: The plug zealot was being
#      hold-positioned BEFORE it reached the wall gap. Two causes:
#      (a) The old code used attack(wall_gap_pos) + hold_position(queue=True),
#          which queued hold_position before the zealot arrived at the gap.
#          FIX: Attack-move to gap, only hold_position when within 0.5 of gap.
#      (b) PART 1 wallgap hold code (any unit within 1.0 of gap gets hold)
#          was also holding the plug zealot as it approached. FIX: Exclude
#          plug zealot from PART 1 hold logic -- it has its own positioning.
#
#  56. PVZ HALLUCINATED PHOENIX DRONE COUNTING + EMERGENCY BATTERIES:
#      When the hallucinated phoenix scouts enemy bases, we track which mineral
#      fields it has seen. When ALL mineral fields at a base are scouted, we
#      count drones and structures (non-main hatchery = worker investment).
#      After the hallucination expires, we compare total enemy workers to our
#      worker SNAPSHOT (taken when the halluc first gets vision of an enemy
#      mineral line). If enemy workers < 90% of our snapshot AND we've fully
#      scouted ALL known enemy bases, we assume an attack is coming and build
#      emergency shield batteries.
#
#      WORKER SNAPSHOT: Our worker count is snapshotted the instant the halluc
#      first sees an enemy mineral field -- NOT when the halluc spawns and NOT
#      when the halluc expires. We keep producing workers during the halluc's
#      flight; comparing against current workers at finalize time inflates our
#      count and makes the enemy always look like they have fewer workers,
#      triggering false attack detection.
#
#      COMPLETE SCOUT REQUIREMENT: Attack detection only triggers if we've
#      fully scouted ALL known enemy bases. If the halluc only scouted 1 of 2
#      known bases before expiring, the missing workers might be at the
#      unscouted base -- we can't conclude they're attacking from partial info.
#
#      Emergency battery positions: From each wall building (gw1, cyber, gw2),
#      go AWAY from the wall midpoint by ~3.5 units (interior/safe side).
#      No emergency pylons -- the wallpylon provides power for all batteries.
#      After all emergency batteries are built, the build order resumes from
#      the saved nf_state.
#
#      Key design: The halluc phoenix path (enemymain → enemynat → enemy3rd → enemy4th)
#      is unchanged. Drone counting runs passively alongside the pathing. Only
#      the FINAL comparison matters -- once the halluc expires or all bases are
#      fully scouted, we make one determination and either build batteries or
#      continue normally.
# =========================================================================
#  67. SHIELD BATTERY BLOCKS GW2-CYBER EXIT GAP: A shield battery placed
#     between gw2 and cyber core can touch both buildings simultaneously,
#     sealing the exit gap and trapping all units inside the natural base.
#     A 2x2 battery and a 3x3 gateway/cyber "touch" when their footprints
#     are adjacent or overlapping: abs(cx - gx) <= 2.5 AND abs(cy - gy) <= 2.5.
#     If a battery touches BOTH gw2 AND cyber, the gap between them is
#     completely blocked — units cannot path out of the natural base.
#     Observed on Persephone AIE: battery at (72,144) touched gw2 (74.5,143.5)
#     and cyber (70.5,141.5), trapping a stalker at (70.4,144.0) for 250+
#     frames (idle, no pathable exit).
#     FIX: Added _battery_touches_wall_gap() helper that checks if a candidate
#     battery position touches both gw2 and cyber. This check is applied in
#     ALL battery placement code paths: find_battery_near_wallpylon(),
#     find_all_battery_positions_near_wallpylon(),
#     _pvz_calculate_emergency_battery_positions(), and every inline
#     cc_pos.towards(gw, -4.5) fallback calculation (9 locations total).
#     When a candidate is rejected, the offset fallback loop continues to
#     search for a safe position nearby.
# =========================================================================
#  68. PVZ ROACH WARREN RESPONSE: ROBO + OBSERVER + IMMORTAL PRODUCTION:
#      When a roach warren is spotted in PvZ, we need:
#      (a) A Robotics Facility for detection (observer vs burrowed roaches)
#          and immortal production (hard counter to roaches).
#      (b) 1 Observer that follows the army (priority: immortal closest to
#          enemymain → stalker closest to enemymain → zealot closest to
#          enemymain) for detection against burrowed roaches and lurkers.
#      (c) Up to 3 Immortals from the robo (immortals deal 40 damage vs
#          armored, roaches are armored — hard counter).
#      (d) 1 Warp Prism after immortals (for reinforcement).
#      The robo is built after twilight council exists (we prioritize twilight
#      for charge research first — chargelots are the backbone of the army).
#      Builder probes tracked via _pvz_robo_builder_tags and excluded from
#      mining via is_worker_locked/get_free_worker.
#
#      CHARGE_STARTED ZEALOT FIX: After charge starts researching, chargelots
#      are effective vs roach-ravager, so the roach warren flag should NOT
#      block zealot production. Changed `if charge_started and not
#      self._pvz_roach_warren_seen` to `if charge_started` — roach warren
#      only blocks zealots BEFORE charge is researching.
# =========================================================================
#  69. PVZ ROACH DEFENSE BLOCKS MASS ZEALOT PRODUCTION AFTER CHARGE:
#      The roach/bane defense section (_roach_defense_active) had a
#      `if charge_started:` branch that produced ONE zealot from ONE
#      warpgate and then returned. This blocked SEQUENCE 4 from mass-
#      producing zealots from ALL idle warpgates. Result: 11 idle
#      warpgates, 10000+ minerals, zero production for minutes.
#      ROOT CAUSE: _roach_defense_active was True whenever
#      _pvz_roach_warren_seen was True (permanent flag). The section
#      was designed for pre-charge production (zealot > sentry > stalker,
#      one at a time), but it kept running after charge started, only
#      producing 1 zealot per frame instead of using all warpgates.
#      FIX: Added `and not _charge_started_rod` to the guard condition.
#      When charge has started, the entire roach defense section is
#      skipped, and SEQUENCE 4 handles mass zealot production from all
#      warpgates (since _pvz_roach_mode becomes False when charge is
#      active, making _produce_zealots_general True).
# =========================================================================
#  70. BUILDER PROBE PHYSICALLY STUCK BETWEEN BUILDINGS: When the builder
#      probe is physically trapped between flower gateways or other
#      structures, it can't path to its build target even though it has
#      a task assigned. The builder stays in place with a MOVE order but
#      never actually moves (position unchanged). The existing stuck
#      counter in is_builder_busy() only catches cases where the builder
#      is AT the target but can't build — it doesn't detect physical
#      pathing failure where the builder can't reach the target at all.
#      FIX: Added PRIORITY 1.1 physical stuck detection in
#      manage_builder_probe_defense(). Tracks builder position history
#      and if the builder hasn't moved >1.0 distance in 7 seconds while
#      having a task AND we can afford the build, the stuck probe is
#      replaced with a new worker from a different location (near the
#      build target or main mineral line). The stuck probe is sent back
#      to mining and marked as released (15s cooldown before reassignment).
# =========================================================================
#  71. PVZ ROACH WARREN: ROBO BEFORE EXTRA GATEWAYS AND CHARGE:
#      When a roach warren is spotted and flower production hasn't built
#      extra gateways yet (only the initial 2 wall gateways exist), the
#      robo should be built ASAP -- even before charge research and before
#      additional gateways. Observer (detection vs burrowed roaches) and
#      immortals (hard counter to armored roaches) are more critical than
#      extra gateways or charge. Once the robo is started, flower production
#      resumes gateway building normally.
#      FIX: (a) manage_pvz_roach_response now checks total_gates <= 2 to
#      skip the twilight prerequisite for robo building. (b) flower production
#      skips gateway building when _pvz_roach_warren_seen is True and robo
#      hasn't been started yet (total_gates <= 2).
#
#  72. PVZ ROACH WARREN: CHRONO PRIORITY ROBO > CHARGE > GATEWAYS:
#      When roach warren/roaches are spotted, chrono boost should prioritize:
#      1. Robotics Facility (while not idle - producing observer/immortals)
#      2. Twilight Council (charge research - critical for chargelots)
#      3. Gateways/Warpgates (fallback)
#      Previously, all chrono went to warpgates, delaying observer/immortal
#      production and charge completion. Against roach timing attacks, every
#      second counts -- getting the observer out 10s earlier can detect
#      burrowed roaches before they wipe our mineral line.
#      FIX: Added roach warren chrono priority checks in both the nexus_first
#      step 3 chrono section and the gateway_first/emergency chrono section.
#
#  73. PVZ ROACH WARREN: 1 ROBO PER ENEMY BASE, GATEWAY SLOTS TRADED:
#      Instead of 1 robo + full gateway count, we build 1 robo per enemy
#      base and reduce the gateway limit accordingly. Example: enemy 3 bases
#      = 3 robos + 8 gateways (instead of 11 gateways). Minimum 2 gateways.
#      Robo count scales with enemy economy -- more bases means more roach
#      production, so we need more immortal output to match.
#      - manage_pvz_roach_response counts enemy hatch/lair/hive to set target
#      - flower_production reduces gateway_limit by robos_remaining
#      - _pvz_try_build_robo excludes existing robo positions to avoid overlap
#      - Immortal target scales with robo count (3 per robo as guideline)
#      - All idle robos produce immortals simultaneously (not just first)
#      - After hitting the scaled immortal target, robos keep producing
#        immortals (no hard cap -- more immortals = better vs roach armies)
#
#      PRODUCTION BEFORE BUILDING: The production section (observer/immortal)
#      runs BEFORE builder cleanup and new robo construction. Previously,
#      the builder cleanup ran first and could delay production by several
#      seconds — the robo would complete but the observer wouldn't start
#      until 7+ seconds later because the code hadn't reached the production
#      section yet. Now production fires on the very first frame the robo
#      completes. Builder cleanup also no longer waits for builder.is_idle
#      (mining probes are never idle) — it releases the builder tag as soon
#      as the robo structure exists.
#
#  74. PVZ ROACH WARREN: GATEWAY LIMIT ACCOUNTS FOR BUILT ROBOS:
#      The gateway limit in manage_flower_production only subtracted
#      _robos_remaining (robos not yet built). Once robos were built,
#      _robos_remaining became 0 and the gateway limit went back to 11,
#      allowing 11 gateways + 2 robos = 13 production buildings.
#      FIX: Now subtracts _effective_robo_count = max(target, current),
#      so gateways + robos combined = base limit (11 or 7). E.g. 2 robos
#      = 9 gateway limit, 3 robos = 8 gateway limit. Minimum 2 gateways.
#
#  75. PVZ ROACH WARREN: ROBO BEFORE GATEWAYS, NO total_gates GUARD:
#      Two places had `total_gates <= 2` checks that prevented the robo
#      from being built urgently and allowed gateways to be spammed:
#      (a) manage_flower_production guard: only blocked gateway building
#          when total_gates <= 2. Once 3rd gateway was built (by the
#          state machine), the guard stopped blocking and flower production
#          spammed gateways while the robo wasn't even started yet.
#      (b) manage_pvz_roach_response _first_robo_urgent: only allowed
#          urgent robo (before twilight) when total_gates <= 2. Same issue.
#      FIX: Removed total_gates check from both locations. When roach
#      warren is seen, the first robo is ALWAYS urgent and flower
#      production ALWAYS blocks gateway building until the robo is started.
#      Also added _pvz_robo_builder_tags to get_free_worker exclusions
#      so the robo builder isn't reassigned by other systems.
# =========================================================================
#  76. PVZ CHANGELING CHASE BUG: Changelings caused the army to abandon
#      its attack push and chase them back to our base without killing
#      them. TWO ROOT CAUSES:
#      (a) _dr_junk_types in the PvZ defense recall (and enemy_near_base
#          in the PvZ defense mode) did NOT include CHANGELING or
#          CHANGELINGZEALOT. Changelings run toward our base by design
#          (Zerg scout units). When they entered the 50-unit detection
#          radius of ourmain/ournat, they were counted as "enemy combat
#          units" and triggered the defense recall, pulling the entire
#          attacking army back from the enemy base. FIX: Added
#          CHANGELING and CHANGELINGZEALOT to _dr_junk_types and the
#          defense mode enemy filter so they never trigger a recall.
#      (b) The defense recall attack commands used
#          unit.attack(enemy.position) instead of unit.attack(enemy).
#          When you attack a POSITION, units move to that spot and shoot
#          things they pass — but a changeling is running AWAY toward our
#          base. The army chases the changeling's last-known position each
#          frame, but the changeling keeps moving, so they just run
#          alongside it without ever attacking. Attack(unit_object) tracks
#          the target and fires when in range. FIX: Changed both defense
#          recall attack commands to use the unit object directly instead
#          of .position. This applies to all enemies in the defense recall,
#          not just changelings — fast-moving units like zerglings and
#          roaches also benefit from direct targeting.
# =========================================================================
#  137. PVZ POST-ROACH-DEFENSE RECOVERY: After successfully defending a
#      roach/ravager rush, the bot was stuck permanently in defense mode.
#      Three cascading problems:
#      (a) _pvz_skip_twilight was permanently True — twilight was never
#          built because the 1-base roach defense intentionally skips it.
#          But manage_flower_production requires twilight to exist before
#          building any infrastructure (gateways, pylons, forge, robo).
#          Without twilight, flower production returns early every frame.
#          Result: 0 gateways, 0 cyber core, 0 forge, 0 robo for the
#          entire rest of the game. Minerals pile up to 8000+.
#      (b) _pvz_1base_roach_defense was permanently True — blocked
#          worker production and affected production logic. The bot never
#          transitioned back to normal play after the defense succeeded.
#      (c) roach_bane_active was permanently True — managed_production_buildings
#          skipped twilight build ("roach-bane state machine handles twilight"),
#          but the state machine had already completed (nf_state=99) and
#          skipped twilight due to _pvz_skip_twilight.
#      FIX: Added _pvz_check_roach_defense_complete() that detects when
#      roach defense is successful (no enemy combat units near our base
#      for 15+ seconds). On success:
#        - _pvz_1base_roach_defense = False
#        - _pvz_skip_twilight = False (so twilight can now be built)
#        - _pvz_worker_production_blocked = False
#        - roach_bane_active = False (so manage_production_buildings builds twilight)
#        - _pvz_post_roach_defense = True (recovery phase marker)
#      The _pvz_post_roach_defense flag:
#        - Allows manage_flower_production to run without twilight (infrastructure rebuild)
#        - Extends _check_cyber_core_rebuild and _check_gateway_rebuild to work
#        - Bypasses sentry requirement for twilight build
#      After defense, the bot rebuilds gateway→cyber→twilight→forge→robo
#      and transitions to the standard immortal/zealot/charge timing attack.
# =========================================================================
#  77. PVT REAPER RESPONSE BUILD STALL + NO SHIELD BATTERY + NO UNIT PRODUCTION:
#      THREE INTERCONNECTED BUGS when the reaper_response state machine gets
#      stuck at state 5 (main pylon):
#      (a) STATE 5 MAIN PYLON STALL: If the main pylon position is blocked
#          (all placement attempts fail), the state machine stays at state 5
#          forever. No GW2 (state 6), no forge (state 8), no
#          twilight (state 9), and no extra gateways get built. The bot
#          also never checks for existing pylons near the main base that
#          could serve the same purpose (e.g., wallpylon, supply pylon from
#          manage_supply_midgame).
#          FIX: Added fallback placement near wallpylon/natural. Also added
#          check for any existing pylon within 15 of ourmain (not just at
#          the specific target position). If all positions fail, skip to
#          state 6 (GW2) — manage_supply builds pylons independently.
#      (b) manage_pvt_shield_battery() EXCLUDED reaper_response: The shield
#          battery function only ran for _pvt_one_base_4gate and gateway_first
#          openings. For reaper_response, it was excluded because state 7 was
#          supposed to handle it. But if state 6 is never reached (state 5
#          stall), there's no backup. The probe that built the nexus sits at
#          the natural mining minerals, safe from the reaper (>10 distance),
#          but is never used for the shield battery.
#          FIX: Added reaper_response as a valid opening for
#          manage_pvt_shield_battery() so it serves as a fallback.
#      (c) SEQUENCE 4 REQUIRES TWILIGHT COUNCIL: manage_army_production's
#          SEQUENCE 4 (main production) requires _seq4_twilight_ok, which
#          checks for a Twilight Council. When the reaper_response state
#          machine is stuck at state 5, no twilight is ever built, so
#          SEQUENCE 4 never fires. After the parallel production completes
#          (adept→sentry→stalker), no more units are produced. The bot
#          sits with 1 gateway and no production for the entire game.
#          FIX: Added PvT reaper_response exception: when _pvt_reaper_active
#          is True and the first three units are done, allow SEQUENCE 4 to
#          produce stalkers even without a twilight council.
# =========================================================================
#  76. PVT CYCLONE LOCK-ON BOUNCE FIX: Stalkers with the LOCKON buff from
#      a cyclone were bouncing between fleeing and attacking every frame.
#      ROOT CAUSE: The anti-cyclone micro checked distance_to(cyclone) > 15
#      BEFORE checking has_buff(BuffId.LOCKON). When a locked-on stalker
#      fled -10 range from the cyclone and ended up >15 away, the distance
#      check caused the buff check to be skipped entirely. The stalker was
#      NOT added to _cyclone_flee_tags, so the sweep/defense micro gave it
#      an attack order instead of respecting the ongoing lock-on. The stalker
#      moved back toward the cyclone, got within 15, triggered the flee
#      again, fled past 15, attack order again... bouncing every frame.
#      FIX: (a) Check has_buff(BuffId.LOCKON) BEFORE the distance cutoff.
#      If the stalker has LOCKON, it ALWAYS gets a flee order regardless
#      of distance from the cyclone. The lock-on persists for the full
#      duration and the cyclone continues dealing damage even if the stalker
#      is far away. (b) Added _cyclone_flee_tags check at the top of the
#      main stalker loop (after retreat tag check), so locked-on stalkers
#      are skipped by ALL micro paths (proxy rax sweep, proxy hidden tech
#      sweep, and wall defense), not just the proxy hidden tech sweep.
# =========================================================================
#  77. PVT PROXY STRUCTURE REPULSION DURING SWEEP: Stalkers during the
#      map sweep were getting stuck near enemy proxy structures close to
#      our base (barracks, factory, etc. within 50 of ourmain). The
#      existing #34 filter removed these structures from attack priorities,
#      but stalkers could still get pulled in by: (a) close-enemy kiting
#      near the structure, (b) auto-attack targeting the nearest structure,
#      or (c) the on-cooldown kiting behavior holding them in place. They'd
#      orbit the proxy structure attacking and kiting instead of pushing
#      toward the enemy base.
#      FIX: Added active proxy structure repulsion in the main stalker loop.
#      When a stalker is within 15 of an enemy structure that's within 50
#      of ourmain, AND the sweep is active, AND no enemy UNITS are within
#      attack range (~7), the stalker moves 15 distance from the structure
#      toward enemynat. The "no enemy units in range" guard ensures we
#      don't blindly run past marines/cyclones that are actively shooting
#      us — we fight those first, then repel from the structure once clear.
#      This applies to BOTH proxy rax and proxy hidden tech sweeps. The
#      repulsion runs before any sweep micro (proxy rax, proxy hidden tech,
#      or wall defense), ensuring stalkers physically move away from proxy
#      buildings near home toward the enemy natural instead of getting stuck
#      fighting them.
# =========================================================================
#  78. PVT SIEGE TANK DIVE ON COOLDOWN: When a stalker is on weapon cooldown
#      and the closest enemy is a siege tank (either mode), the old logic
#      kited AWAY from it to 6 range. This is catastrophic vs siege tanks
#      in siege mode — they have 13 range and a ~2 minimum range dead zone.
#      Kiting away keeps the stalker at 6 range, well within the siege
#      tank's killing zone. The siege tank fires every 3 seconds dealing
#      40 damage (25 splash) — it will kill the stalker in 3-4 shots
#      while the stalker can only shoot back once per cooldown cycle.
#      FIX: When on weapon cooldown and the closest enemy is a SIEGETANK
#      or SIEGETANKSIEGED, move TOWARD the tank to close the gap and get
#      inside its minimum range (~2). Once inside minimum range, the tank
#      can't fire and the stalker gets free shots when cooldown expires.
#      This applies to both the proxy rax sweep and proxy hidden tech
#      sweep on-cooldown sections. Non-siege-tank enemies still kite
#      normally (6 range, away from enemy).
# =========================================================================
#  79. PVT PATH CHECK + STARPORT TECHLAB PRIORITY: Three changes to the
#      proxy hidden tech sweep micro:
#      (a) PATH CHECK INTEGRATION: Uses Cython PathChecker (BFS on the
#      pathing grid) to detect whether stalkers can walk into the enemy
#      main base. When supply depots block a ramp, the pathing grid has
#      a gap and BFS returns False. Once the depot is destroyed, the
#      game updates the pathing grid and the next frame's check returns
#      True — automatically setting _pvt_ramp_breached. This is more
#      reliable than just tracking whether a specific depot tag was
#      destroyed (which misses multi-depot walls where destroying one
#      isn't enough). The PathChecker is initialized once (lazily) and
#      cached in self._path_checker. Falls back to the old depot tag
#      tracking if PathChecker is unavailable (import failed).
#      (b) DEPOT ON COOLDOWN: When fighting the depot to break into
#      the enemy base, on weapon cooldown stalkers move TOWARD the depot
#      (not kite away). The depot doesn't shoot back — there's no reason
#      to kite from it. Moving toward it maintains vision on high ground
#      and keeps pressure up. Only exception: cyclone lock-on kiting.
#      After depot is killed and path is clear: on cooldown, move toward
#      enemymain to close the gap and push into the base.
#      (c) STARPORT TECHLAB PRIORITY: When we find a starport with a
#      techlab attached, we kill the TECHLAB FIRST (Priority 2), before
#      the starport building itself (Priority 3). The techlab enables
#      banshee cloak and BC tactical jump — the two most dangerous
#      abilities in proxy hidden tech. If we kill the starport but the
#      techlab survives, the Terran can lift it and attach to a new
#      starport, retaining cloak/jump. Killing the techlab FIRST
#      permanently denies these abilities. Once the techlab is dead,
#      normal priorities resume (starport → other structures → enemymain).
# =========================================================================
#  80. PVT PHASE 1 MISSING DEPOT TARGETING + SIEGE TANK DIVE:
#      Phase 1 of the proxy hidden tech sweep was just blindly attack-moving
#      to enemynat with no micro at all. Two critical gaps:
#      (a) DEPOT TARGETING: When stalkers reached the enemy main ramp and
#      found depots blocking the path, they kept attack-moving to enemynat
#      instead of targeting the depots. The depot focus-fire logic only
#      existed in Phase 2+, but the phase transition (closest stalker
#      within 5 of enemynat) often doesn't trigger while stalkers are at
#      the ramp (10-15 units from the natural position). Stalkers would
#      sit at the bottom of the ramp, attack-moving to enemynat, unable
#      to break through the wall. FIX: Added depot focus-fire to Phase 1
#      — same logic as Phase 2 Priority 0 (closest depot to enemymain,
#      vision gate, move toward depot on cooldown, cyclone exception).
#      (b) SIEGE TANK DIVE: Phase 1 had no weapon cooldown handling.
#      Stalkers on cooldown just stood still while a siege tank shelled
#      them. The dive logic (#78) only existed in Phase 2+. FIX: Added
#      siege tank dive and close enemy kiting to Phase 1's weapon
#      cooldown handling. On cooldown: dive toward siege tanks, kite
#      from other close enemies, or attack-move to sweep target if
#      no close enemies.
# =========================================================================
#  81. BUILDER PHYSICAL STUCK DETECTION FALSE POSITIVE AT BUILD TARGET:
#      The physical stuck detection (Priority 1.1 in manage_builder_probe_defense)
#      was replacing probes that were intentionally waiting at their build target
#      position. In the reported case, the builder probe was at (70,142) with
#      task=four_gate_chain, target=(70.5, 141.5) (the cybercore position). It
#      was correctly holding position, waiting for the gateway to complete so it
#      could immediately build the cyber core. But the stuck detection saw "hasn't
#      moved in 7 seconds + can afford the build" and replaced the probe with a
#      new one from the mineral line. The replacement had to walk 40+ units back
#      to the cyber position, delaying the cyber core by 10+ seconds. Worse, the
#      replacement then got damaged by a reaper and was replaced AGAIN (HP-based
#      replacement #20), causing further delays.
#      FIX: Before declaring the builder physically stuck, check if it's already
#      within 3 units of its build target. If so, the builder is intentionally
#      waiting at the right position for a prerequisite structure to finish — it
#      is NOT stuck. Only trigger the replacement when the builder is far from
#      the target and not making progress, which indicates a genuine pathing
#      failure (e.g., physically trapped between buildings).
# =========================================================================
#  82. DEPOT MOVE TARGET ON UNPATHABLE GROUND: When stalkers move toward a
#      supply depot blocking the enemy ramp, stalker.move(depot_target) sets
#      the move target to the depot's CENTER position. But the depot building
#      occupies that space, making it unpathable ground. The SC2 pathing
#      engine redirects the stalker AROUND the depot, causing oscillation —
#      the stalker tries to walk into the depot, gets pushed around it, tries
#      again, gets pushed back. This results in massive attack resets (363
#      MOVE overriding ATTACK events in one game) as the stalker bounces
#      between move and attack orders every frame.
#      FIX: Replace stalker.move(depot_target) with stalker.move(
#      depot_target.position.towards(stalker.position, 1)). This sets the
#      move target to a point 1 unit from the depot toward the stalker,
#      which is always on pathable ground on the stalker's side. The stalker
#      moves to this position and can then attack the depot from range
#      without oscillating. Applied to ALL depot focus-fire sections: proxy
#      rax PRIORITY -1, proxy rax Priority 3, proxy hidden tech Phase 1,
#      proxy hidden tech Phase 2 Priority 0, and main army ramp depot.
# =========================================================================
#  43. PVZ HATCH-FIRST ROACH WARREN: ADEPT/ZEALOT INSTEAD OF STALKER:
#      In hatch-first PvZ games, the roach warren can be spotted by the
#      scout BEFORE roach_bane_active is set. The pool finishes late in
#      hatch-first (121s+), so the early-pool + gas detection that sets
#      roach_bane_active never triggers. The _pvz_roach_warren_seen flag
#      IS set correctly, but nothing in manage_army_production checks it
#      when _roach_defense_active is False. This causes THREE cascading
#      bugs:
#      (a) State 67.5 trains adepts despite roach warren (no check)
#      (b) State 72 trains 2 adepts despite roach warren (no check)
#      (c) SEQUENCE 4 produces zealots (the roach/bane defense section
#          that produces stalkers never runs because _roach_defense_active
#          is False)
#      (d) Gas transfer pulls gas workers after twilight (designed for
#          zealot/charge path needing only 100 gas), starving stalker
#          production which needs continuous 50 gas per unit.
#      FIX (4 changes):
#      (a) _roach_defense_active now includes _pvz_roach_warren_seen
#      (b) State 67.5: train stalkers instead of adepts when roach warren seen
#      (c) State 72: skip to state 73 when roach warren seen (stalkers
#          produced by manage_army_production roach/bane defense section)
#      (d) manage_gas_transfer: skip gas pull when _pvz_roach_warren_seen
# =========================================================================
#  57. PVZ ADEPT PRODUCTION WHEN ROACH WARREN SEEN: Multiple code paths
#      trained adepts even after the roach warren was spotted. Adepts are
#      terrible against roaches (melee shade, low DPS vs armored, get kited
#      by ranged roach fire). When _pvz_roach_warren_seen is True, ALL adept
#      production should be replaced with stalker production. Five locations
#      were missing this check:
#      (a) manage_second_adept_defense(): trained adepts from idle gateways
#          when lings were near the wall, regardless of roach warren. This is
#          the most impactful fix since it runs every frame independently of
#          the state machine. When roach warren is seen, it now produces
#          stalkers instead. Also added roach detection near the wall.
#      (b) State 66.71, 66.72, 66.73: parallel adept training while building
#          shield batteries in the lings-spotted path. No roach warren check.
#          Now produces stalkers when roach warren is seen.
#      (c) State ~66.8 (adept training in lings-spotted path): same issue.
#      (d) SEQUENCE 4 general production: In PvZ, always produced zealots
#          (_produce_zealots_general = not self.vs_terran). Added
#          _pvz_roach_mode check: when roach warren seen AND charge hasn't
#          started, produce stalkers instead of zealots. After charge starts,
#          chargelots are effective against roach-ravager.
# =========================================================================
#  58. PVZ PRODUCTION STALL + GAS TRANSFER + HALLUCINATION SCOUTING:
#      Multiple issues causing the bot to float 1000+ minerals/200+ gas with
#      idle gateways and zero stalker production:
#      (a) SEQUENCE 4 guard required `already_pending_upgrade(CHARGE) == 1.0`
#          (charge COMPLETE) in Part B. With 0 stalkers and charge only at 8%,
#          Part B was False → SEQUENCE 4 never fired → total production deadlock.
#          FIX: Changed to `> 0` (charge researching OR complete).
#      (b) After 2 adepts in hatch-first no-roach-warren path, there was NO
#          stalker production path. SEQUENCE 3 should have fired, but with the
#          Part B deadlock, the entire production fell through to nothing.
