#          FIX: Added sentry anti-cyclone micro to the non-proxy-hidden-tech
#          sentry defense section (manage_pvt_stalker_defense). Also updated
#          the threshold from < 10.0 to <= 12.0 (proactive) in both paths.
#          The 12-distance threshold gives a buffer so the sentry starts
#          moving before the cyclone enters lock-on range (~7).
#      (b) STALKER NO ON-COOLDOWN MICRO IN NON-PROXY-HIDDEN-TECH DEFENSE:
#          The stalker defense micro (manage_pvt_stalker_defense) for
#          gateway_first and reaper_response paths had no on-cooldown
#          stutter-step logic. Stalkers just issued attack() and stood
#          still on cooldown, making them sitting ducks for cyclones and
#          siege tanks. The proxy hidden tech wall defense (note #130) had
#          this logic, but it wasn't ported to the general defense path.
#          FIX: Added on-cooldown stutter-step micro to Priority 1 (main),
#          Priority 2 (nat), and Priority 3 (wall) targeting sections:
#          - Cyclone/Siege tank: move TOWARD on cooldown (pressure/dive)
#          - Other enemies within 7: kite back to max range (6)
#          - Enemies beyond 7: attack-move toward them
#      (c) PROBE BOUNCING ON SHIELD BATTERY REBUILD (STATE 10):
#          When the shield battery was destroyed and the rebuild code in
#          state 10 fired, it pulled a new worker every frame because
#          builder_locked was NOT set. Other systems (manage_supply,
#          _pvt_build_supply_pylon_if_needed) would hijack the builder,
#          canceling the build order. Next frame, already_pending was 0
#          again (build was cancelled), so the rebuild code fired again
#          with a new worker — causing infinite bouncing.
#          FIX: Set builder_locked = True when assigning the rebuild task.
#          Also check if builder_current_task is already "battery" before
#          re-issuing the build command — if the builder is alive and
#          working, don't pull a new worker. Clear the task only if the
#          builder died.
#      (d) ADEPT STANDS STILL ON WEAPON COOLDOWN VS REAPER:
#          The adept reaper chase code used attack() in both the
#          "weapon ready" and "on cooldown" branches. When the adept is
#          within attack range (6) but on weapon cooldown, attack() causes
#          it to stand still waiting for cooldown to expire instead of
#          closing distance. This makes the adept a sitting duck for the
#          reaper, which can shoot and run while the adept waits.
#          FIX: Changed the on-cooldown branch to use move() toward the
#          reaper's position instead of attack(). This makes the adept
#          close distance on cooldown so it's closer when cooldown expires
#          and can shoot again. Off cooldown, attack() still works (fires
#          if in range, or move+fire if out of range).
