# =========================================================================
#  138. PVT ADEPT IGNORES REAPER — ARMY MOVEMENT OVERRIDE: When a reaper
#     enters our base during proxy hidden tech or reaper_response, the
#     adept should shade/attack the reaper (handled by
#     manage_pvt_stalker_defense adept shade code). But
#     manage_army_movement includes ADEPT in the army variable and gives
#     it MOVE orders every frame (to the army position or sweep target).
#     These MOVE orders override the shade/attack orders from the adept
#     micro code, leaving the adept wandering aimlessly while the reaper
#     kills workers unchecked. Observed in a PvT game: adept existed at
#     t=150s+, reaper visible since t=120s, but zero adept micro output
#     (no shade, no attack, no chase). The adept was being swept into
#     manage_army_movement's army positioning logic and given MOVE orders
#     that canceled any micro from manage_pvt_stalker_defense.
#     FIX: Added adept exclusion from the army variable in
#     manage_army_movement when: (a) vs_terran, (b) proxy hidden tech
#     or reaper_response opening, AND (c) a reaper is within 25 of
#     ourmain or 15 of ournat. The adept shade/chase code in
#     manage_pvt_stalker_defense handles the adept's micro instead.
#     Same pattern as the banshee defender stalker exclusion — tags_not_in.
# =========================================================================
#  140. PVT PROXY HIDDEN TECH BUILD ORDER: GW1 > NEXUS > CYBER > GAS1 > GAS2
#      > MAIN PYLON > GW2. Previously, gateway_first built gw2 immediately
#      when proxy marauder was detected (1 gas before barracks). When it
#      later upgraded to proxy hidden tech (2nd gas spotted), gw2 was already
#      built, giving the build order: gw1 > gw2 > nexus > cyber > gas1 > gas2.
#      This was suboptimal — nexus was delayed, slowing our 2-base economy.
#      FIX: Removed gw2 (and states 2.1, 7, 8) from gateway_first entirely.
#      The gateway_first state machine now only builds: gw1 > gas1 > gas2 >
#      cyber > transition. The 4-gate state machine handles everything after:
#      nexus (state 1.5) > cyber (state 4) > gas1 (state 2) > gas2 (state 3)
#      > main pylon (state 5) > gw2 (state 6) > battery (state 7) > adept+sentry > ...
#      For proxy rax, the 4-gate state machine's state 3.7 builds gw2 before
#      gases (same as before). Only proxy hidden tech was affected.
# =========================================================================
#  141. PVT PROXY HIDDEN TECH: NEXUS BEFORE CYBER AND GAS IN GATEWAY_FIRST.
#      Previously (DEV NOTE #140), gateway_first built gw1 > gas1 > gas2 >
#      cyber for ALL paths (including proxy hidden tech), then transitioned
#      to the 4-gate state machine which built nexus at state 1.5. However,
#      the 4-gate entry point calculation skipped state 1.5 (nexus) entirely
#      when cyber already existed, entering at state 5 (main pylon) instead.
#      This meant nexus was NEVER built during the opening for proxy hidden
#      tech — a critical bug that left us on 1 base for the blink stalker
#      timing.
#      FIX: Restructured gateway_first to build nexus FIRST for proxy hidden
#      tech, right after gw1. New build order: GW1 > NEXUS > CYBER > GAS1 >
#      GAS2 > transition to 4-gate (main pylon > gw2). This ensures nexus
#      is built ASAP for the 2-base blink stalker economy.
#      New states added: 2.1 (wait nexus/pre-move cyber), 2.2 (build cyber),
#      2.3 (wait cyber/pre-move gas), 2.4 (build gas1 without 60s delay).
#      The parallel cyber pre-move (line ~29098) is disabled for proxy hidden
#      tech since the nexus→cyber chain handles its own pre-moving.
#      The state 6 transition now checks if nexus exists and routes the 4-gate
#      entry point accordingly: if nexus exists → state 5 (main pylon); if not
#      → state 1.5 (build nexus first, fallback path).
# =========================================================================
#  139. PVT REMOVE PROXY STRUCTURE REPULSION / BYPASS: The proxy structure
#      repulsion (#77) and structure bypass (#34) code moved stalkers AWAY
#      from enemy structures toward the enemy base during sweeps. This was
#      originally added to prevent stalkers from getting stuck fighting proxy
#      buildings near our base instead of pushing out. However, this behavior
#      now conflicts with our attack timing — we WANT stalkers to kill enemy
#      structures they encounter, including proxy buildings near our base,
#      rather than blindly pushing past them.
#      REMOVED:
#      (a) PROXY STRUCTURE REPULSION block (was before proxy rax sweep micro):
#          Moved stalker 15 distance from any structure within 50 of ourmain
#          toward enemynat. Completely removed.
#      (b) #34 filter in proxy rax sweep Priority 6: Filtered out structures
#          within 50 of ourmain from attack priorities. Removed the filter —
#          stalkers now attack structures near our base normally.
#      (c) #34 filter in proxy hidden tech sweep Priority 4: Same filter as
#          (b). Removed — stalkers attack nearby structures regardless of
#          distance from ourmain.
#      (d) On-cooldown near-our-base push (proxy hidden tech Phase 2):
#          When stalker was within 50 of ourmain and on weapon cooldown, it
#          moved toward enemymain instead of kiting. Removed — stalkers now
#          kite normally from close enemies even near our base.
#      (e) "Skip stalkers already fighting" near-base override: When a
#          stalker was already attacking something within 50 of our base
#          during sweep, it was overridden with attack-move toward enemy
