#      which deactivates _hatch_first_active entirely and activates
#      _roach_defense_active (which handles pure stalker production).
#      FIX: Changed Step 2 to produce adepts up to 4, then stalkers.
# =========================================================================
#  152. PVZ ROACH WARREN: 3RD AND 4TH GAS FOR DUAL ROBO:
#      With 2+ robos producing observers (75g), immortals (100g), and
#      warp prisms (100g), 2 gas geysers (~240 gas/min) is not enough.
#      Robos would idle waiting for gas, dramatically reducing immortal
#      output. With 4 gas (~480 gas/min), both robos can continuously
#      produce immortals and observers without gas starvation.
#      BOTH 3rd AND 4th gas trigger immediately when the 2nd robo is
#      started (pending or completed). Dual robo needs max gas right
#      away — staggering delays production. Built in
#      manage_pvz_roach_response() using get_free_worker() with the
#      _pvz_gas34_started flag to prevent duplicate builds.
#      Gas workers auto-managed by manage_gas_workers().
# =========================================================================
#  153. PVZ HYDRA RESPONSE: ROBO BAY + COLOSSUS + ALTERNATING PRODUCTION:
#      When Hydralisks or Hydralisk Dens are detected (_pvz_hydra_seen),
#      we need Robotics Bay and Colossus production. Colossus hard-counter
#      hydras (extended thermal lance outranges hydra fire, splash shreds
#      hydra masses).
#
#      Detection: _check_hydra() checks for HYDRALISKDEN structures and
#      HYDRALISK units. Sets _pvz_hydra_seen flag (permanent).
#
#      Build chain:
#      1. No robo facility → build one (via _pvz_try_build_robo)
#      2. Robo facility exists, no robo bay → build ROBOTICSBAY
#      3. Both exist → produce colossus/immortals with alternating ratio
#
#      Production ratio (alternating to keep balanced):
#        - immortal_count > colossus_count → make colossus
#        - colossus_count > immortal_count → make immortal
#        - tied → make immortal (immortals more versatile vs roaches too)
#        - Always ensure 1 observer before combat units
#
#      Integration with roach warren production: When hydra is detected
#      AND robo bay is ready, the roach-only production section is skipped
#      (the hydra section handles alternating colossus/immortal instead).
#      The charge research section still runs normally (chargelots are
#      important vs hydra/ling compositions too).
#
#      The function guard is also updated: manage_pvz_roach_response()
#      now activates when EITHER roach warren OR hydra is detected.
# =========================================================================
#  154. PVT NAT BATTERY POSITION: TOUCHING GW1+CYBER (SAME AS PVP) +
#      BUILDER PROBE BOUNCE FIX:
#      (a) BATTERY POSITION: The old PvT nat shield battery position used
#      find_battery_near_wallpylon() which placed the battery relative to
#      the wallpylon, typically 6-7 units from gw1/cyber. Against 1-base
#      bio timing attacks, the battery was too far from the wall fight —
#      stalkers couldn't kite back to it between shots. The PvP battery
#      position uses find_pvp_battery_position() which places the battery
#      edge-adjacent to both gw1 and cyber core (on the inside of the
#      wall). This position lets stalkers shoot at the wall gap, take a
#      hit, step 2 tiles back to the battery, heal, and re-engage. Now
#      PvT uses the same find_pvp_battery_position() as the primary
#      placement, with find_battery_near_wallpylon and cyber→gw -4.5 as
#      fallbacks. Both manage_pvt_shield_battery() and reaper state 7
#      were updated.
#      (b) BUILDER PROBE BOUNCE: manage_pvt_shield_battery() runs
#      independently of the reaper_response state machine. When the state
#      machine was at state 6 (building GW2), manage_pvt_shield_battery()
#      stole the builder probe by setting builder_current_task="battery"
#      and builder_task_target=battery_pos. The state machine's pre-move
#      kept moving the probe back to gw2 position. The probe bounced
#      between gw2 (147.5, 102.5) and battery (154, 104) for 28 seconds,
#      delaying GW2 from t=120s to t=156s. Against a 1-base bio timing,
#      this 36-second delay in getting GW2 up meant only 1 gateway for
#      production during the critical defense window.
#      FIX: Added guard in manage_pvt_shield_battery() that skips the
#      battery build when the reaper state machine is at state 7 or
#      earlier. DEV NOTE #160/#167: State 6 is now GW2 and state 7 is
#      battery, so the guard uses state 7 (battery) to prevent
#      double-building — the state machine handles battery at state 7
#      directly, and this function only serves as a fallback after
#      state 7.
# =========================================================================
#  155. PVZ THREE FIXES: PROBE HALT, SENTRY ENERGY RECHARGE, MAP SWEEP:
#      (a) PROBE HALT NOT CLEARED AFTER DEFENSE: The hallucination attack
#      detection (DEV NOTE #56) sets _pvz_probe_production_halted and
#      _pvz_worker_halt_confirmed when enemy workers < 95% of ours. These
#      flags are ONLY cleared by a subsequent hallucination confirming
#      enemy workers >= 95%. But against an all-in enemy, workers stay
#      low forever, so the flags are never cleared — even after the roach
#      defense completes (15s no enemies near base). The roach defense
#      complete function clears _pvz_worker_production_blocked and
#      _pvz_early_rw but NOT _pvz_probe_production_halted. Result:
#      workers permanently stuck at 26 for the rest of the game.
#      FIX: Also clear _pvz_probe_production_halted and
#      _pvz_worker_halt_confirmed in _pvz_check_roach_defense_complete().
#      (b) SENTRY ENERGY RECHARGE SKIPPED BY DEFENSE CHRONO: The PvZ
#      worker count defense chrono (all chrono to gateways) returned
#      early, which skipped the sentry energy recharge code placed after
#      it. Sentry spawned with 50 energy, needed 75 for hallucination,
#      but never got energy recharged. Had to wait ~32 seconds for
#      natural regen. Late hallucination = late scouting = couldn't
#      confirm when to resume probe production.
#      FIX: Moved sentry energy recharge BEFORE the defense chrono so
#      it runs first. Energy recharge uses a different nexus ability
#      (ENERGYRECHARGE not CHRONOBOOST) so it doesn't conflict. Also
#      reset _pvz_sentry_energy_charged when no sentry exists (died),
#      so a replacement sentry gets energy recharged.
#      (c) MAP SWEEP ARMY SPLIT: When no enemy structures were visible,
#      the sweep code only issued attack-move to units without orders.
#      Units with existing attack orders kept targeting their old
#      positions (enemynat vs enemymain), splitting the army. The
#      advancement threshold was 5 units (too loose), and the sweep
#      didn't restart when reaching the end.
#      FIX: All units attack-move to the SAME sweep target. Advance
#      when ANY unit reaches within 1 of the target. Restart sweep
#      from 0 when reaching the end. Same fix applied to sentry-lead
#      path, no-sentry path, and the valid_targets empty fallback.
# =========================================================================
#  156. PVZ EARLY ROACH WARREN PROBE CAP: When a roach warren is scouted
#      before 2:30 (150s) via hallucinated phoenix or probe scout, the
#      enemy is going for an early roach timing attack. We must cap probes
#      at 34 to save minerals for units, shield batteries, and pylons.
#      Every probe beyond 34 costs 50 minerals that delays a stalker by
#      ~2.5 seconds. 34 probes = enough for 16 mineral workers + 6 gas
#      workers + 12 oversaturation at natural, which is sufficient to
#      sustain stalker/immortal production without starving the army.
#      If we already have more than 34 probes (including in-production)
#      when the roach warren is spotted, cancel all in-production probes
#      immediately to reclaim their 50 mineral cost. This is similar to
#      the proxy marauder probe cap at 23, but less extreme since we
#      have a natural nexus and need a larger economy for roach defense
#      (immortals, robo, shield batteries all cost significant minerals).
#      The time threshold (150s) distinguishes early aggression (2-base
#      roach timing at ~4:00-5:00) from later roach transitions where
#      we should continue probe production for a macro game.
#      Implementation: _pvz_roach_warren_seen_time records when the roach
#      warren was first spotted. build_workers() checks this time and
#      enforces the 34 probe cap when roach warren was seen before 150s.
# =========================================================================
#  157. PvP HIDDEN 4-GATE DEFENSE: When forge_first is chosen in PvP
#      because no enemy buildings are visible (no forge, no gateway, no
#      expansion), the opponent is likely hiding a 4-gate zealot rush.
#      The old build order went straight from gas2 to supply pylon to
#      stargate, but against a 4-gate zealot rush, voidrays arrive too
#      late. We need ground army first.
#      NEW BUILD ORDER (no enemy buildings visible, no proxy near base):
#      Forge > GW1 > GW2 > Cannon > Nexus > Pylon > Cyber > Gas1 > Gas2
#      > 2 Zealots (chrono gateways) > 4 Stalkers > Defense Pylon > Voidray
#      Implementation:
#      (a) _pvp_no_enemy_buildings flag set when no enemy forge/gateway/
#          nexus is visible at the 51s decision point.
#      (b) execute_wall_off "no proxy" sub-path skips supply_pylon_step
#          when _pvp_no_enemy_buildings (cyber_step=9 instead of 10).
#      (c) manage_army_production produces 2 zealots then 4 stalkers
#          before any other production when _pvp_no_enemy_buildings is
#          True and transition hasn't happened yet.
#      (d) _pvp_cannon_rush_transition gates on having 2 zealots + 4
#          stalkers before transitioning. Also builds a defense pylon
#          (for stargate power) before completing the transition.
#      (e) Chrono: ALL chrono goes to gateways producing zealots/stalkers
#          during the defense phase. No nexus probe chrono. Added as a
#          dedicated section in the forge_first/emergency chrono path,
#          before the general gateway chrono. After defense units are done,
#          falls through to normal chrono allocation.
#      (f) manage_supply_midgame EXCLUDED during hidden 4-gate defense:
#          When _pvp_no_enemy_buildings is True and the transition hasn't
#          completed, manage_supply_midgame returns early. The user reported
#          "too many pylons" because this function was building extra pylons
#          that interfered with the defense build order. The wall_off state
#          machine handles the main pylon, and the transition code handles
#          the defense pylon — no other pylon building should occur.
#  158. PVP STALKER BATTERY LEASH: DON'T RETREAT IF ALREADY BEING SHIELDED:
#      Stalkers within 7 range of a shield battery are already getting their
#      shields recharged. Retreating further to battery_pos is wasteful — they
#      should keep attacking as long as they stay within the 7-range leash.
#      Only stalkers BEYOND the leash need to retreat.
#      ALSO: When a stalker is retreating to battery on weapon cooldown and
#      an enemy enters weapon range with weapon off cooldown, the stalker
#      should attack that target. On cooldown, continue moving to battery.
#      ALSO: Idle stalkers should move directly to stalker_rally (5 range
#      toward map center from battery) instead of the incremental "towards"
#      approach that caused stalkers to get stuck near gw1 position. The
#      old code moved only 3 range at a time, so newly-spawned stalkers
#      near gw1 never reached the battery rally point.
#  159. PVP ADEPT SHADE NOT CHASED + ZEALOTS ATTACK PROBES:
#      (a) The PvP stalker defense code had NO adept shade (ADEPTPHASESHIFT)
#      handling. Shades near our base were invisible to the stalker micro,
#      so the adept teleported into our mineral line freely. Fixed by adding
#      a new Layer 1.5 that detects shades near ourmain (15) / ournat (10)
#      and targets them with smart() — even beyond the battery leash. The
#      shade has a 4-second timer so it's now-or-never. Stalkers still
#      shoot enemies in weapon range while moving toward the shade.
#      (b) Zealots during the voidray push used smart_follow(lead_vr) which
#      relies on SC2 auto-acquisition. Auto-acquisition targets the nearest
#      enemy, which is often probes instead of the enemy stalkers shooting
#      at our voidrays. Fixed: zealots now explicitly target the nearest
#      ground combat unit (excluding workers) within 12 range of the lead
#      voidray. Only fall back to smart_follow when no combat units are
#      nearby.
#  160. PVP ATTACK TIMING FIXES — FORGE, RALLY, SENTRY LEAD, GUARDIAN SHIELD:
#      (a) Forge at gw3 was NOT being destroyed before the PvP attack push.
#      manage_army_movement() returns early for pvp_voidray (line 16041), so
#      the forge destruction code at line 17820+ was never reached. Fixed by
#      adding a forge-at-gw3 check in _pvp_voidray_attack() BEFORE the push
#      starts. Both our own forge and enemy forge at gw3 are targeted.
#      (b) Stargates had no rally points — newly produced voidrays sat idle
#      at the stargate until the attack logic picked them up. Fixed: stargates
#      now rally to the army leader (sentry > stalker > zealot) so voidrays
#      fly to the army immediately upon production.
#      (c) During the attack push, voidrays and stalkers now follow the sentry
#      (when one exists) instead of independently attack-moving. The sentry
#      leads the push, keeping the army ball cohesive so guardian shield
#      covers everyone. The army_leader is determined as: sentry > stalker >
#      zealot > lead voidray.
#      (d) Sentry activates guardian shield when enemy combat units are within
#      6 range of the lead voidray. This protects the entire army ball from
#      ranged damage during engagements.
#  161. PVT CC-FIRST DETECTION + NEXUS-FIRST INTO REAPER_RESPONSE:
#      Three interconnected changes for PvT CC-first detection:
#      (a) Worker counting: Changed _pvt_track_scv_near_enemy_main from
#          20-radius to 50-radius. Now counts SCVs within 50 of enemy main
#          PLUS SCVs within 50 of our main (only if no enemy structure is
#          within 50 of our main — proxy SCVs building structures don't
#          count). This gives accurate worker counts for CC-first detection.
#          Example: 14 SCVs at enemy main + 1 scouting SCV at our base
#          (not building) = 15 total → CC-first. But if that SCV IS
#          building a structure, it's a proxy and doesn't count = 14.
#      (b) CC-first detection: When no barracks + no gas by 60s AND
#          worker count >= 15 AND scout probe is alive → set _pvt_cc_first.
#          The build order changes to nexus-first: Nexus → GW1 → Cyber →
#          Gas → Gas → etc. (standard reaper_response goes GW1 → Nexus →
#          Cyber → Gas → Gas). Added reaper_response state 1.5 to build
#          GW1 after nexus. Gateway_first is suppressed when _pvt_cc_first
#          is set (it goes to state 99 immediately).
#      (c) PvT minimum 23 probes: Added worker_limit minimum of 23 for
#          all PvT openings in build_workers(). Also updated the four_gate
#          probe cap to 999 for PvT so manage_workers handles the limit.
#      (d) Charge timing attack pathing: PvT reaper_response now uses a
#          different sweep order: enemy4th → enemy3rd → enemynat →
#          enemymain → remaining bases. Vision-based advancement: if we
#          can see the current waypoint but no enemies are there, advance
#          to the next waypoint immediately. Updated sweep_index checks
#          for _pvt_main_destroyed, army_wipe_retreat, and siege_tank
#          retreat to account for the different sweep order (4 enemy bases
#          before our bases instead of 2).
#  162. PVT BUILDER PROBE MANAGEMENT FIXES:
#      Four fixes for PvT builder probe behavior during the reaper_response
#      build chain. These address the issues where:
#        - Helper probes returned to mining instead of replacing the builder
#        - Builder tasks were lost during enemy worker retaliation
#        - GW2 was delayed by an unnecessary sentry gate
#        - Shield battery was delayed because it came after GW2
#        - Builder idled while waiting for gateway to finish
#      (a) HELPER→BUILDER SWAP: When the builder probe is attacked by an
#          enemy worker and health drops below 90% (the old helper trigger),
#          instead of pulling a "helper" probe to fight alongside the builder,
#          we now immediately SWAP: the helper becomes the new builder, and
#          the damaged builder goes back to mining. This ensures the building
#          continues uninterrupted with a healthy probe. The old helper
#          approach caused the helper to return to mining (carrying minerals)
#          after the fight, losing the build task entirely. Updated the
#          cleanup code to recognize when the helper IS the builder (after
#          a swap) and not release it.
#      (b) RETALIATION TASK PRESERVATION: In is_builder_busy(), when the
#          builder's current ability is ATTACK, the code previously always
#          cleared the builder's task (builder_current_task=None). This was
#          intended for PvP cannon rush chase probes "hijacking" the builder,
#          but it also cleared the task during legitimate retaliation against
#          enemy scout workers. After the fight, the builder had no task to
#          resume and idled. Fix: if self._builder_in_combat is True (builder
#          is retaliating against enemy workers near base), preserve the task
#          and return True. Only clear the task when the ATTACK is from a
#          non-retaliation source.
#      (c) GW2 BEFORE BATTERY (reverted from DEV NOTE #160): Originally the
#          order was "GW2 (state 6) → Battery (state 7)". DEV NOTE #160 swapped
#          this to "Battery (state 6) → GW2 (state 7)" for faster wall defense.
#          However, the 2nd gateway provides critical production capacity during
#          the early defense window that outweighs the marginal benefit of an
#          earlier battery. DEV NOTE #167 reverted to the original order:
#          "GW2 (state 6) → Battery (state 7)". The sentry gate (removed in
#          DEV NOTE #161) stays removed — GW2 builds when affordable with
#          cyber core, no waiting for adept/sentry. Updated all state
#          transition references, pre-move logic, and fallback guards.
#      (d) BUILDER PRE-MOVE IN STATE 2: In reaper_response state 2 (build
#          cyber core), after the nexus completes, the state machine waits
#          for the gateway to finish before building cyber. Previously, the
#          builder just sat idle during this wait (sometimes 20+ seconds).
#          Added pre-move logic: while waiting for the gateway, the builder
#          moves toward the cyber core position so it's ready to build
#          immediately when the gateway finishes.
# =========================================================================
#  163. PVT BUILDER PROBE stop() + GW1 REUSE + FORGE SENTRY GATE + BATTERY FALLBACK:
#      Four fixes for remaining PvT builder probe issues:
#      (a) REPLACEMENT PROBE stop() BEFORE MOVE: When a builder probe is
#          replaced (HP-based, SWAP, or stuck), the replacement probe is
#          pulled from the mineral line and may have active HARVEST_GATHER
#          or HARVEST_RETURN orders (carrying minerals). Without stop(),
#          the mining system overrides the replacement's move command on
#          the next frame — the replacement bounces between the build
#          target and the mineral line, never actually building. This is
#          the same class of bug as DEV NOTE #51 (PvZ shield battery
#          builder bounce). Fixed by adding replacement.stop() BEFORE
#          replacement.move(target_pos) in all three replacement paths:
#          Priority 1 (HP < 50%), Priority 1.1 (physical stuck), and
#          Priority 1.3 (SWAP under attack).
#      (b) GW1 BUILDER REUSE FOR NEXUS: When the reaper_response state
#          machine reaches state 1 (build nexus) and the tracked
#          _pvt_reaper_probe_tag is stale (probe died or missing), the
#          old code called get_free_worker(nat_pos) which picked the
#          closest mining probe. But the probe that just built gw1 might
#          be sitting idle at the gw1 position — it's the obvious choice
#          to continue the single-probe chain. Fixed: before falling back
#          to get_free_worker(), search for a probe near gatewall1 (within
#          5 distance). If found and not locked by another system, assign
#          it as the reaper chain probe. Also added stop() before move()
#          for probes with active mining orders.
#      (c) FORGE SENTRY GATE REMOVED: State 8 (forge) had a gate that
#          waited for _pvt_sentry_trained before building the forge. This
#          delayed the entire tech chain (forge → twilight → charge) by
#          30+ seconds when the sentry was delayed by resource constraints
#          (adept first in production, minerals tight). The sentry is
#          trained in parallel by the production loop and should NOT block
#          the build chain. Fixed: removed the sentry gate entirely. The
#          forge builds as soon as GW2 is done and we can afford it.
#      (d) SHIELD BATTERY FALLBACK TIMEOUT: manage_pvt_shield_battery()
#          previously returned early when _reaper_state_sb <= 6, blocking
#          the fallback entirely even when the state machine was stuck at
#          an earlier state for 30+ seconds (e.g., state 5 pylon stall).
#          Fixed: Changed the check to only block when state is exactly 6
#          (actively building battery). For states 1-5, added a 15-second
#          timeout after cyber core completion — if the state machine
#          hasn't reached state 6 within 15s of cyber completing, the
#          fallback builds the battery independently. This ensures the
#          shield battery is never delayed more than 15s after cyber,
#          regardless of state machine stalls. Also tracks cyber
#          completion time in _pvt_cyber_complete_time.
# =========================================================================
#  164. PVZ ADEPT ATTACK PUSH + CHANGELING HANDLING:
#      Two issues from a PvZ game:
#      (a) ADEPTS NOT MOVING OUT WITH THE ATTACK: In the hatch-first
#          no-lings path, _manage_adept_no_lings() holds adepts at the
#          3rd base with hold_position(). When attack timing triggers,
#          the function returns immediately without issuing any move
#          orders — the adepts stay idle at the 3rd base for the entire
#          game while the rest of the army pushes. The sentry-lead sweep
#          only picks up units within ~15 distance of the sentry, which
#          is too close for adepts that are 25+ away at the 3rd.
#          FIX: When attack timing triggers, _manage_adept_no_lings()
#          now issues move(sentry) or move(army_center) to all adepts
#          that are far from the army group. This gets them moving
#          toward the push, and once they reach the sentry's range,
#          the sweep code takes over with follow/attack orders.
#      (b) CHANGELINGS NEAR OUR BASE: Three sub-problems:
#          (1) The builder probe flee logic treats changelings as "combat"
#              units (they're not in WORKER_TYPES), causing the builder
#              to flee from harmless scouts. This triggered 34 pylon
#              redirects in one game as the builder kept fleeing a
#              ChangelingZealot near the build site.
#              FIX: Added changelings to the harmless types list in the
#              builder flee logic so the builder ignores them.
#          (2) The base defense code correctly excludes changelings from
#              threat detection, but this means NO units attack changelings
#              near our base — they just walk around freely, providing the
#              Zerg with free vision for the entire game.
#          (3) When the army DID try to attack changelings, it used
#              attack-move on a POSITION. Changelings keep moving, so the
#              army attacks where the changeling WAS, not where it IS.
#              FIX: Added manage_changeling_hunter() that assigns the
#              closest free worker to attack the changeling UNIT directly
#              (not position). Workers deal 5 damage per hit and can kill
#              a changeling in 8-10 hits — only ~3 seconds. The worker is
#              locked via _changeling_hunter_tag (excluded from mining by
#              is_worker_locked()) and returns to mining after the changeling
#              dies. Only activates for changelings within 25 of our bases.
#              The army is freed to focus on destroying the enemy base.
# =========================================================================
#  165. PVZ ROACH DEFENSE: BATTERY PRIORITY + ADEPT 3RD BASE + WALLGAP HOLD:
#      Three issues from a PvZ roach defense game:
#      (a) SHIELD BATTERY PRIORITY: During 1-base roach defense, the bot spent
#          minerals on gateways, forge, and twilight instead of shield batteries.
#          Only 1 battery was near the wall while 8+ gateways and 3 robos were
#          built. The roach defense code says "5+ batteries" but the extra
#          battery builder (manage_pvz_extra_batteries) was gated behind
#          minerals >= 100 while gateways cost 150 each — the flower production
#          system kept spending minerals on infrastructure before batteries.
#          FIX: Added shield battery gates in manage_production_buildings
#          (skip twilight) and manage_flower_production (skip gateways) until
#          3+ shield batteries exist. Also lowered the mineral threshold for
#          battery building from 100 to 50 during roach defense.
#      (b) ADEPT RETREAT TO 3RD BASE: In the hatch-first no-lings path,
#          adepts were shading to the 3rd base even when a roach attack was
#          hitting the natural. The "no_threats" check only looked for
#          zerglings near the wall/3rd, not roaches or macro intel. Adepts
#          need to stay at the defense line when enemies are at ournat.
#          FIX: Modified _manage_adept_no_lings() Phase 1 (initial shade
#          dispatch) and Phase 5 (shade-to-3rd logic) to only send adepts
#          to the 3rd base if enemies are within 15 of our3rd. If enemies
#          are at ournat but not our3rd, adepts move toward the defense
#          line instead of shading away.
#      (c) STALKER HOLD POSITION BLOCKING PUSH: The wallgap hold_position
#          logic was putting ALL units near the wall gap on hold_position,
#          including stalkers. This prevented stalkers from pushing out to
#          engage roaches at range. Hold position should only apply when
#          zerglings are actually threatening to push through the gap.
#          FIX: Added _lings_near_wallgap check — wallgap hold_position
#          now only activates when zerglings are within 10 of the wall gap.
#          Against roaches (no lings), stalkers are free to push out and
#          fight. The _roaches_near_wall_no_lings flag already handled
#          part of this, but the hold_position was still being applied
#          when roaches weren't yet within 10 of the wall.
#  166. PVT CHARGE GAS RESERVATION — STALKERS BLOCKING CHARGE RESEARCH:
#      When +1 armor starts researching and twilight council is ready (or
#      pending), stalkers were being produced from all available gateways,
#      draining all gas and preventing charge research from starting. In
#      the logged game, armor started at t=239s, twilight was ready at
#      t=190s, but charge didn't start until t=569s — a 330-second delay.
#      The root cause: SEQUENCE 4 in manage_army_production produces
#      continuous stalkers (50 gas each) when it's PvT and charge hasn't
#      started. With 3-7 gateways running, gas never accumulated to 100.
#      PvZ already had charge gas reservation (DEV NOTE #77/#109), but
#      PvT had no equivalent. The fix reserves 100 gas for charge when:
#        (a) It's PvT
#        (b) Charge hasn't started researching
#        (c) Twilight Council exists or is pending
#      If producing a stalker (50 gas) would drop vespene below the 100
#      gas reserve, the stalker is skipped. This applies to both the
#      SEQUENCE 4 general production path and the proxy rax forge_first
#      "Step 3" stalker production path. The air threat path already had
#      charge gas reservation (min_gas_for_stalker += 100).
# 167. PVT REAPER RESPONSE: GW2 BEFORE BATTERY (revert DEV NOTE #160):
#      Reverted the build order from "Battery (state 6) → GW2 (state 7)"
#      back to "GW2 (state 6) → Battery (state 7)". The 2nd gateway
#      provides critical production capacity during the early defense
#      window — with only 1 gateway, the bot can't produce enough units
#      to defend against Terran bio pressure. The shield battery follows
#      immediately after in state 7. The sentry gate removal from
#      DEV NOTE #161 is preserved — GW2 still builds when affordable
#      with cyber core, no waiting for adept/sentry. Updated all state
#      transition references, manage_pvt_shield_battery() fallback
#      guard (now checks state 7 instead of state 6), pre-move comments,
#      and build order strings.
# 168. PVT MEDIVAC DROP DEFENDERS + ATTACK RETREAT FIX:
#      Two issues from a PvT game where the army retreated unnecessarily:
#      (a) MEDIVAC DROP DEFENSE: Added _pvt_medivac_defender_tags system,
#          mirroring the banshee defender system. When medivacs are within
#          25 of ourmain or ournat, 3 stalkers per medivac (up to 6 max)
#          are assigned to attack the medivac. These defenders are excluded
#          from the main attack army, the stalker pool, and combat army,
#          just like banshee defenders. This prevents medivac drops from
#          causing a full army retreat — the small defense force handles
#          the drop while the main army keeps attacking.
#      (b) OBS < 2 RETREAT FIX: Previously, if an observer was destroyed
#          during an attack (dropping obs count below 2) while air threat
#          was detected, the entire army retreated for "detection safety".
#          But the banshee/medivac defender system was already handling
#          the air threat — the defenders can see and shoot cloaked
#          banshees. Now, if attack timing is triggered and obs < 2, we
#          check if there are active defenders (banshee + medivac). If
#          there are 3+ defenders, the army continues pushing. Only if
#          there are fewer than 3 defenders does the army retreat.
# 169. PVT CC-FIRST NEXUS BOUNCE BUG FIX (DEV NOTE #162):
#      When CC-first was detected, the reaper_response state machine built
#      the nexus using a NEW probe (assigned at 400 minerals), while the
#      gw_first pre-moved probe sat idle at gw1. After building the nexus,
#      state 1.5 immediately issued probe.move(gw1_pos), which fought with
#      is_builder_busy() re-issuing move(ournat) because builder_current_task
#      was still "nexus" at ournat — causing the probe to bounce between
#      ournat and gw1 forever, never building the gateway.
#
#      FIX (three parts):
#      (a) REUSE GW_FIRST PROBE: When CC-first is detected, the gw_first
#          pre-moved probe (already at gw1) is transferred to reaper_response
#          via _pvt_reaper_probe_tag instead of assigning a new one. A new
#          state 0.5 moves this probe from gw1 to ournat at 350 minerals
#          (15 SCVs already confirmed by _pvt_cc_first), so it arrives
#          before 400 minerals and can build the nexus immediately.
#      (b) CLEAR NEXUS TASK AFTER PLACING: For Protoss, the probe is free
#          after placing a building. After probe.build(NEXUS, ournat),
#          builder_current_task and builder_task_target are cleared
#          immediately for CC-first (instead of staying as "nexus" at ournat).
#          Then queue: gather(nearest_mineral, queue=True) → move(gw1_pos,
#          queue=True) so the probe mines in between building tasks and
#          arrives at gw1 ready to build the gateway.
#      (c) STATE 1.5 NO-Override: State 1.5 no longer issues probe.move()
#          when it can't afford the gateway — the probe is already heading
#          to gw1 via the queued orders. Only issues move() if the probe is
#          idle with no orders and far from gw1 (fallback for lost orders).
#          Also adds a guard: if the nexus hasn't been placed yet, returns
#          to state 1 instead of overriding the build command.
#  170. PVT CC-FIRST PIVOT — Gateway before Nexus when gas/barracks spotted
#      after CC-first decision (DEV NOTE #164):
#      When CC-first is detected (15+ SCVs, no gas, no rax), the bot
#      commits to building the nexus before the gateway (reaper_response
#      states 0.5 → 1 → 1.5). However, if a Refinery or Barracks is then
#      spotted near the enemy main BEFORE the nexus has been placed, the
#      Terran is NOT doing CC-first — they're doing a standard reaper
#      expand. A reaper is coming and we need the gateway IMMEDIATELY.
#
#      Without this pivot, the bot waits for 400 minerals to build the
#      nexus first (22+ seconds in the observed game), then builds the
#      gateway, resulting in zero defense against the reaper.
#
#      FIX: Added a pivot check at the top of execute_pvt_reaper_response()
#      that detects when _pvt_cc_first is True AND state is 0.5 or 1 AND
#      nexus hasn't been placed yet AND (enemy_gas_near_main or enemy_
#      barracks_near_main). On pivot:
#        (a) Clear _pvt_cc_first, set _pvt_cc_first_pivot
#        (b) Clear stale nexus builder task (prevents bounce)
#        (c) Redirect probe from ournat to gw1 position
#        (d) Jump to state 1.5 (build gateway FIRST)
#      State 1.5 is modified: when _pvt_cc_first_pivot is True, the nexus
#      guard is skipped (nexus shouldn't exist yet), and after the gateway
#      is built, it transitions to state 1 (build nexus) instead of state 2
#      (cyber core). This gives the build order: Gateway → Nexus → Cyber,
#      which is the standard reaper_response order that prioritizes defense.
# 171. PVZ HALLUCINATED PHOENIX DRONE COUNTING FIX — Accumulate tags, not snapshots:
#      The hallucinated phoenix scout was dramatically undercounting enemy drones.
#      In the observed game: nat had 15 drones (counted 0), 4th had 2 drones
#      (counted 0), main had ~19 (counted 16). Total: 16 out of ~36 actual.
#
#      ROOT CAUSE: The code was taking a SNAPSHOT count — counting only the drones
#      currently visible and within 12 distance of the base position at the exact
#      tick when all mineral fields were first marked as scouted. By the time the
#      last mineral field got tagged, the phoenix had already flown past the drone
#      cluster, so most drones were no longer visible or within range.
#
#      The code already did the right thing for mineral fields: it accumulated
#      mineral field tags into a set (_pvz_halluc_scouted_minerals) over time as
#      the phoenix flew over them. But for drones, it took a one-time snapshot.
#
#      FIX: Added _pvz_halluc_scouted_drones dict (same pattern as _scouted_minerals)
#      mapping base_key to a set of drone tags. Every tick, any visible drone within
#      12 distance of the base position gets its tag added to the set. When all
#      minerals at a base are scouted, the drone count is len(set) instead of a
#      snapshot. This correctly captures every drone seen at any point during the
#      phoenix's flight over each base, not just the ones visible at the snapshot.
#
#      Also removed structure-to-worker conversion. The limitation is larvae over
#      time, not minerals — a spawning pool or extractor doesn't represent a "worker
#      that could have been." Structures are still counted and logged for info but
#      are NOT added to the total enemy worker count.
# 172. PVP DT DEFENSE: Sentry after 3 stalkers, forge + cannons, oracle + revelation:
#      When the hallucinated phoenix scout (sent by the sentry after 3 stalkers)
#      spots an enemy Dark Shrine or Templar Archive, the bot activates DT defense:
#
#      PRODUCTION: Gateway order changed from stalker→stalker→(conditional sentry)
#      to stalker→stalker→stalker→sentry. The sentry provides hallucinated phoenix
#      scouting to detect DT tech early.
#
#      DT DEFENSE BUILD (states 20-25, parallel with main build chain):
#      20 = Forge at natural (inside toward main, doesn't block entry)
#      21 = Pylon behind mineral lines (midpoint of main+nat, away from center by 10)
#      22 = Cannon between main nexus and mineral line (touching nexus, in pylon power)
#      23 = Cannon between nat nexus and mineral line (touching nexus, in pylon power)
#      24 = Cannon touching shield battery + gw1 (front wall defense)
#      25 = Complete
#
#      ORACLE: When DT is detected, the first idle stargate produces an oracle
#      before resuming voidray production. The oracle provides revelation to
#      detect cloaked Dark Templar.
#
#      ORACLE MICRO:
#      - Default: Follow lead voidray > lead stalker > lead zealot
#      - If invisible unit within 25 of ourmain or ournat: move to enemy, cast
#        revelation when within 12 range (energy >= 25)
#      - During attack timing: follow lead stalker, cast revelation on any
#        invisible enemy within 12 range
# 173. PVT IDLE ARMY RALLY AT SHIELD BATTERY + 5 TOWARD MAP CENTER:
#      In PvT vs 1-base bio rush, army units started inside the base and got
#      stuck in the wall when trying to move out to defend. The root cause:
#      wall_rally was set to the cybercore/wallpylon position (INSIDE the wall),
#      so idle stalkers stood behind the wall. When the bio rush arrived, units
#      tried to path through the wall gap and got stuck, unable to defend.
#
#      FIX: Three changes to position idle army at shield_battery + 5 toward
#      map center (OUTSIDE the wall, within battery shielding range of 7):
#        (a) wall_rally in manage_pvt_stalker_defense: When a shield battery
#            is ready, set wall_rally to battery_pos + dir_to_center * 5.0
#            instead of cybercore/wallpylon. Idle stalkers move OUTSIDE the
#            wall to the battery rally point, ready to attack immediately.
#        (b) _pvt_rally_to_wallpylon: When battery is ready, rally sentries/
#            adepts to battery+5 instead of wallpylon. Same reasoning — units
#            outside the wall can fight immediately without wall-stuck issues.
#        (c) Gateway rally points (update_rally_points): In PvT, when battery
#            is ready, new units rally to battery+5 instead of toward ournat.
#            Force re-rally when battery first completes (clear rally_points_set).
#            This ensures newly produced stalkers walk directly to the front.
# 174. PVT PRE-ATTACK RALLY DIRECTION: MAP CENTER VS ENEMYMAIN:
#      Pre-attack rally positions (cybercore+5/7) used cyber_pos.towards(em_pos, N)
#      which points toward the enemy main base. On some maps, the angle from
#      cybercore toward enemymain goes INTO the wall instead of through the ramp
#      gap, causing units to split on either side of the wall — some inside,
#      some outside, unable to group up. FIX: Changed all three pre-attack rally
#      calculations to use cyber_pos.towards(map_center, N) instead. Map center
#      always points OUTSIDE the wall toward the ramp, consistent with the
#      battery+5 toward map center rally from DEV NOTE #173. Affected locations:
#        (a) Warp prism hold prep positions (zealot_prep_wp, stalker_prep_wp)
#        (b) Sentry warp prism wait position (stalker_prep_wp)
#        (c) Pre-attack rally positions (pre_attack_rally_zealot/stalker/fallback)
# 175. GAS BUILDER WORKERS: RETURN TO MINERALS AFTER BUILDING:
#      When gas builders finished constructing an assimilator, they were
#      released (tag set to None) but not sent back to mineral mining.
#      SC2 auto-sends the builder into the assimilator it just built, but
#      a DIFFERENT set of workers gets assigned as gas miners by
#      manage_gas_workers(). The builder probe idled for 21+ seconds.
#      FIX: Before releasing the gas builder tag, find the probe and send
#      it to the nearest nexus via smart() so it returns to mineral mining.
#      This temporarily adds 4 workers to minerals (builder + 3 gas miners
#      assigned by manage_gas_workers) but self-corrects within 1 mining
#      trip. Applied to all 6 gas builder release points: gw_first gas1/2,
#      reaper gas1/2, 4-gate gas1/2.
# 176. PVT ZEALOT PRODUCTION DURING CHARGE GAS RESERVE:
#      In PvT, before charge starts, SEQUENCE 4 produces stalkers but
#      reserves 100 gas for charge research. When gas was too low to afford
#      a stalker (gas - 50 < 100 reserve), the gateway was skipped entirely
#      — no unit was produced. This caused gateways to sit idle for 20+
#      seconds during the tech research phase while minerals piled up.
#      FIX: When the stalker gas reserve blocks stalker production, produce
#      a zealot instead (0 gas cost). Zealots don't delay tech timing and
#      provide early defense. They become chargelots once the upgrade
#      completes, so they're not wasted investment.
# 177. PYLON BUILDER REDIRECT BUG — RELEASE ON STRUCTURE APPEARANCE:
#      When a pylon structure appeared (under construction, not yet ready),
#      is_builder_busy() cleared the pylon task and builder_locked flag.
#      This freed the builder immediately, allowing manage_flower_production
#      to assign a NEW pylon position. The move() to the new position
#      cancelled the current pylon build (SC2 cancels build orders when
#      the probe moves away). The probe then bounced between the two
#      positions — one frame building at position A, next frame redirected
#      to position B — until one pylon eventually completed by chance.
#      Evidence from log: at t=208.4s, builder had PROTOSSBUILD_PYLON at
#      (53,49) with locked=False; by t=209.2s, flower production assigned
#      a new pylon at (52,44), cancelling the first build.
#      FIX: Two changes to only release the builder when the pylon is READY
#      (complete), not when it first appears (under construction):
#        (a) is_builder_busy pylon check: Only clear the pylon task when
#            the pylon is is_ready. Under-construction pylons keep the
#            builder locked and committed, preventing reassignment.
#        (b) manage_flower_production pylon lock: Only clear _flower_pylon_ordered
#            when the pylon is is_ready, not just when it exists.
# =========================================================================

# 178. PVP CANNON RUSH DEFENSE — NEXUS TIMING, ZEALOT CAP, AND PROBE BOUNCE FIX:
#      Three issues when defending a cannon rush where only pylons blocked
#      the natural (no cannons or gateways completed near our base):
#      (a) NEXUS TIMING: When enemy pylons blocked the natural position,
#          the bot immediately skipped the nexus step and went cyber/gas.
#          However, our own cannon + 1 zealot typically destroys the
#          blocking pylon BEFORE we reach 400 minerals. By waiting at
#          the nat position instead of skipping, we can place the nexus
#          immediately once the pylon is cleared — no delay. Only if we
#          reach 400 minerals and can_place still fails (area still
#          blocked) do we fall back to cyber/gas.
#          FIX: Removed the immediate skip for enemy pylons near nat.
#          The probe now moves to nat and waits. If can_place fails at
#          400 minerals, then skip to cyber/gas as fallback.
#      (b) ZEALOT CAP: The zealot cap was always 2 during cannon rush
#          defense. But when the enemy only built pylons near us (no
#          cannons or gateways completed), 2 zealots is wasteful — a
#          single zealot can clear pylons fine, and the 100 minerals
#          saved gets us to nexus faster.
#          FIX: If no enemy cannons or gateways are near our base, cap
#          zealots at 1 instead of 2. If cannons or gateways exist near
#          our base, keep the cap at 2 (need more defense).
#      (c) NEXUS PROBE BOUNCE: In _pvp_cannon_rush_transition(), the
#          nexus builder was obtained via get_free_worker() each frame
#          without tracking the probe tag or locking it. Worker
#          management would reassign the probe to mining between frames,
#          causing it to bounce between the nat position and mineral
#          fields. The nexus was never built.
#          FIX: Added _pvp_cannon_rush_nexus_probe_tag to track the
#          assigned probe, set locked_for_nexus=True on it so worker
#          management leaves it alone, and re-use the same probe on
#          subsequent frames. Added the tag to is_worker_locked() and
#          get_free_worker() exclusions. Also added pre-move logic
#          (deposit resources + move to nat) so the probe walks to the
#          position instead of trying to build from across the map.
#          Lock is released once the build order is issued or if
#          can_place fails (position still blocked).
# =========================================================================

# 179. PVT EARLY PROXY RAX DETECTION, CANNON TARGETING, AND BUILDER FIXES:
#      (a) EARLY PROXY RAX DETECTION: Previously, the bot waited until 60s
#          to detect proxy rax in PvT (Rule 3: no barracks + no gas + <15 SCVs
#          at 60s → forge_first). But by 45s, the scout has already confirmed:
#          mineral line complete, both gas geysers scouted with no refinery,
#          supply depot seen, no barracks, and only 14 SCVs. All the info
#          needed to conclude proxy rax is available ~15s earlier. Waiting
#          until 60s meant the forge wasn't ordered until t=62s and didn't
#          complete until t=94s — by which time the bunker was already built
#          at t=87s. Detecting at ~45s means the forge starts at ~47s and
#          completes at ~79s, so our cannon can kill the SCV before the
#          bunker finishes.
#          FIX: Added Rule 2.7 — if enemy_main_minerals_complete AND
#          _pvt_both_gas_geysers_scouted AND no gas AND no rax AND depot
#          seen AND <15 SCVs → forge_first immediately (no 60s wait).
#      (b) CANNON TARGETING PRIORITY: SC2 cannons auto-acquire the closest
#          target, which means they shoot at bunkers/structures instead of
#          the SCV building them. Killing the SCV first prevents the bunker
#          from completing. Added _manage_cannon_targeting() that forces
#          cannon attack priority: SCVs > enemy combat units > structures.
#          Only issues attack commands when a higher-priority target exists
#          (avoids spamming every frame). Active during forge_first
#          (emergency_wall_active) for PvT and PvP cannon rush defense.
#      (c) SCV TAG-BASED COUNTING: The _pvt_scv_peak_near_main counter
#          was based on counting visible SCVs near the enemy main. When our
#          probe killed an SCV during scouting, or when SCVs left vision to
#          build proxy structures, the count would drop, potentially
#          preventing proxy rax detection. FIX: Added _pvt_scv_tags_seen
#          set that permanently records SCV tags. Once a tag is counted,
#          it stays counted even if the SCV dies or leaves vision. The
#          tag-based count (len of the set) is the authoritative source
#          for proxy rax and CC-first detection.
#      (d) BUILDER SWAP IMMUNITY: After swapping a damaged builder for a
#          fresh replacement, the replacement would immediately get swapped
#          out too if it took damage from the same enemy worker. In the log,
#          two consecutive swaps happened at 88% HP just 6 seconds apart,
#          pulling two probes off their jobs. FIX: Added 15-second swap
#          immunity after each swap. The replacement probe is expected to
#          win the fight (the first probe already damaged the enemy), so
#          it should fight through rather than being pulled out again.
#          Also changed the replacement behavior from stop→move→attack
#          to stop→attack(target_pos) so the probe attack-moves toward
#          the build location while fighting enemies along the way.
#      (e) PRE-MOVE STATE MAPPING FIX: The pre-move section in
#          execute_pvt_reaper_response() had the wrong state-to-building
#          mapping. The pre-move assumed state 6=battery, state 7=GW2
#          (from an older build order), but the actual code has state 6=GW2,
#          state 7=battery. This caused the probe to pre-move to the WRONG
#          position at each state transition, bouncing between the battery
#          position and gatewall3. Specifically, while building the battery
#          (state 7), the pre-move checked already_pending(GATEWAY) which
#          was true (GW2 still under construction) and sent the probe to
#          gatewall3, while the state handler tried to move it to the battery
#          position. FIX: Corrected the pre-move state mapping:
#          state 5 (pylon) → GW2 position, state 6 (GW2) → battery
#          position, state 7 (battery) → forge position. Also fixed the
#          docstring to match the actual state numbering.
# 180. ORACLE REVELATION ABILITY ID: The correct ability ID for Oracle
#      Revelation is AbilityId.ORACLEREVELATION_ORACLEREVELATION.
#      NEVER use AbilityId.ORACLE_REVELATION -- it does NOT exist in the
#      AbilityId enum and will crash with AttributeError. This follows the
#      same pattern as the shield battery ability (note #1): the sc2 Python
#      library uses the full duplicated-name format for ability IDs.
#      (Also see _pvp_oracle_micro / try_revelation for the usage site.)
# 181. THREE PvZ ISSUES — FORGE PLACEMENT, 3RD BATTERY, GATEWAY/ROBO BALANCE:
#      Three bugs found in a PvZ hatch-first game vs roach warren:
#      (a) PvZ FORGE TOUCHES NAT NEXUS EDGE TILES: The PvZ forge
#          placement (states 67.7, 70.25, and 70.6) excluded wall buildings
#          (gw1, gw2, cyber, wallpylon, battery) but did NOT exclude the
#          natural or main nexus edge tiles. The forge was placed between
#          the mineral line and the natural nexus at (111.5, 141.5), blocking
#          probes. The PvT reaper response forge (DEV NOTE #129) already has
#          proper AABB exclusion with 5.5 min axis distance from nexus centers.
#          FIX: Added nexus edge tile exclusion (5.5 AABB) to all three PvZ
#          forge placement sites (67.7, 70.25, 70.6), same pattern as PvT.
#          Also applied the same fix to the PvP DT defense forge (state 20).
#      (b) 3RD SHIELD BATTERY PERMANENTLY SKIPPED BY 1 SCOUTING ZERGLING:
#          _check_3rd_nexus_under_attack() sets _3rd_nexus_under_attack=True
#          when ANY enemy is within 15 of our3rd. A single scouting zergling
#          at t=196s set this flag permanently — state 67.6 skipped the 3rd
#          battery and NEVER re-attempted it, even after the zergling left.
#          The 3rd base had no shield battery the entire game.
#          FIX: In state 67.6, re-check whether enemies are STILL near the
#          3rd base when the flag is set. If enemies have left (0 visible
#          within 15 range), clear the flag and proceed with battery
#          construction. Only skip the battery if enemies are currently
#          present, not based on a stale flag from 20+ seconds ago.
#      (c) PvZ ROACH WARREN: ROBO SPAM + GATEWAY STARVATION = MINERAL FLOAT:
#          The gateway_limit formula was gateway_limit = max(2, base - robo_count).
#          When the bot built excessive robos (up to 17 in one game!), the
#          gateway limit dropped to 2 — the absolute minimum. With 2000+
#          minerals and only 2 gateways, the bot couldn't spend minerals.
#          Root causes: (1) No hard cap on robo count — _target_robo_count
#          was max(1, enemy_bases) but stale builder tracking meant robos
#          kept being ordered. (2) The minimum of 2 gateways is way too low
#          — chargelot warpgate waves need 5+ gateways minimum to be a
#          meaningful mineral sink alongside gas-heavy robo production.
#          FIX: Three changes:
#          - Hard cap on robo count at 3 (in manage_pvz_roach_warren and
#            hydra response). 3 robos can't consume more than ~300 gas/min,
#            which is the max from 3-base gas income. Extra robos sit idle.
#          - Cap _effective_robo_count at 3 for the gateway_limit formula
#            (even if somehow more robos exist, don't subtract them).
#          - Raise gateway minimum from 2 to 5 — we always need gateway
#            production for chargelot waves to absorb mineral income.
# 182. THREE MORE PvZ ISSUES — EMERGENCY BATTERY, SHIELD BATTERY DEFENSE, WORKER HALT:
#      (a) EMERGENCY BATTERY INDEX ADVANCES BEFORE BUILD CONFIRMED: In
#          manage_pvz_emergency_batteries(), builder.build() was called and the
#          index immediately incremented. But build() just queues a command —
#          the builder can be hijacked by another system before the structure
#          appears. The battery was lost forever because the index had already
#          moved past it. In the replay, the emergency battery at (110, 139)
#          was ordered but the builder was hijacked (HARVEST_GATHER) the same
#          frame — the battery never appeared and was never retried.
#          FIX: Don't advance the index when build() is called. Instead, wait
#          until the structure actually appears in game state (checked by the
#          existing "already exists" check at the top of the function). Also
#          added a pending check so we don't re-order while a battery is
#          already in the build queue.
#      (b) SHIELD BATTERY DEFENSE ONLY CHECKS IF ANY BATTERY EXISTS: In
#          manage_shield_battery_defense(), the check was "if
#          self.structures(SHIELDBATTERY): return" — meaning ANY battery
#          ANYWHERE would prevent building more. A battery at the 3rd base
#          (89, 142) that was too far from the wall to provide shielding
#          blocked replacement of the destroyed nat battery at (114, 138).
#          After the nat battery was destroyed by roaches, no replacement
#          was built because the 3rd-base battery still existed.
#          FIX: Changed the check to only look for batteries within 10 units
#          of gatewall1 (near the wall). A battery at the 3rd base doesn't
#          prevent rebuilding the wall battery.
#      (c) WORKER PRODUCTION PERMANENTLY HALTED BY WORKER-COUNT DEFENSE:
#          The hallucination scout worker-count detection sets
#          _pvz_probe_production_halted=True, but this flag was only cleared
#          by (1) a subsequent hallucination confirming workers >= 95%, or
#          (2) roach defense completing (_pvz_check_roach_defense_complete).
#          But the roach defense completion check only ran if
#          _pvz_1base_roach_defense or roach_bane_active was set. If the
#          attack was detected via worker count but the roach-warren-specific
#          flags were never set (e.g. the zerg went ling/bane instead), the
#          completion check never ran and workers stayed halted forever.
#          In the replay, workers stopped at t=224.5s and never resumed,
#          ending with only 2 workers at game end.
#          FIX: Extended _pvz_check_roach_defense_complete() to also trigger
#          when only _pvz_probe_production_halted is set (without roach
#          defense flags). If no enemies are near base for 15 seconds, the
#          worker halt is cleared regardless of which defense mode triggered
#          it.
# =========================================================================
# =========================================================================

# 180. PVZ FORGE-FIRST / GATEWAY-FIRST ECONOMY AND BUILD INTEGRITY FIXES:
#      Five bugs discovered in a PvZ forge-first game where the bot went
#      gateway_first (14 enemy workers = 5-15 range → gateway_first path):
#      (a) PROBE PRODUCTION CAP AT 16: The build_workers() function has
#          explicit overrides for forge_first (worker_limit=23), nexus_first
#          (worker_limit=17), and vs_terran (worker_limit=23), but NO
#          override for gateway_first in PvZ. The formula gives 16 with
#          1 base + 0 gas, and nothing raises it. Probe production stops
#          at 16 permanently until the natural nexus completes (~90s later).
#          FIX: Added gateway_first + vs_zerg override: worker_limit = 23.
#      (b) +1 WEAPONS WITHOUT TWILIGHT: In manage_flower_production(), the
#          +1 Ground Weapons research (line 14885) had NO twilight council
#          check — it only checked vs_zerg + forge exists + can afford.
#          When the twilight builder got hijacked, the wall forge started
#          +1 weapons before twilight existed. Charge is far more important
#          than +1 weapons, so weapons should wait for twilight.
#          FIX: Added twilight exists/pending check before starting +1
#          weapons research.
#      (c) ROBO BUILD NEVER RETRIES: When _pvz_try_build_robo() issues a
#          worker.build(ROBOTICSFACILITY, pos) but another probe builds a
#          pylon that blocks the position, the build silently fails. The
#          builder tag stays in _pvz_robo_builder_tags and
#          _pvz_robo_count_started never decrements (builder is alive).
#          The system thinks "a robo is being built" forever and never
#          retries. In the game, robo=0 persisted from t=258s to t=416s.
#          FIX: Added stale builder detection — if builder has been tracked
#          for >5s but no robo structure or pending robo exists, remove the
#          builder from tracking and decrement the count. Added
#          _pvz_robo_builder_timestamps dict to track when builds were
#          ordered.
#      (d) STALE _emergency_to_standard_done FLAG: The flag is set when
#          twilight becomes pending, but if the build is cancelled (builder
#          hijacked), it stays True forever. This bypasses the twilight
#          prerequisite in manage_flower_production, which allowed the +1
#          weapons research to start without twilight. In the game, the
#          twilight builder was hijacked at t=186.3s ("Builder hijacked
#          (HARVEST_GATHER) while far from twilight") and the flag was
#          never cleared — twilight was still at 0 even at t=406s.
#          FIX: In manage_production_buildings(), if
#          _emergency_to_standard_done is True but twilight doesn't exist
#          and isn't pending, reset the flag and re-trigger
#          _emergency_needs_twilight so the twilight build gets retried.
#      (e) GATEWAY DOUBLE-QUEUE: A gateway can have a second unit queued
#          before the first finishes. The is_production_ready() function
#          used gw.is_idle for regular gateways, but in some observation
#          race conditions, is_idle may be True on the same frame a unit
#          was just queued. Also, _pvz_defense_training() used
#          gateways.ready.idle without checking orders.
#          FIX: Updated is_production_ready() to check BOTH is_idle AND
#          len(gw.orders) == 0 for regular gateways. Also updated
#          _pvz_defense_training() to filter with the same check.
# =========================================================================
# 181. PVZ FORGE-FIRST / GATEWAY-FIRST TWILIGHT INTEGRITY FIXES:
#      Three additional issues discovered after DEV NOTE #180 fixes:
#      (a) +1 WEAPONS RACE CONDITION: The DEV NOTE #180 fix used
#          already_pending(TWILIGHTCOUNCIL) to gate +1 weapons research.
#          But already_pending() returns True on the frame a build is
#          ORDERED, even if the builder gets hijacked and the build is
#          cancelled the same frame. In the game log, +1 weapons started
#          at t=186.3s — the exact frame twilight was ordered and the
#          builder was immediately hijacked. already_pending was True
#          for that one frame only. FIX: Changed to use
#          self.structures(TWILIGHTCOUNCIL).amount > 0 which only counts
#          buildings that physically exist (build_progress > 0), not
#          merely "pending" orders that may fail.
#      (b) _emergency_to_standard_done RACE: Same already_pending()
#          race condition at line 6048 and 12069. The flag was set True
#          on the frame twilight was "pending", then the build was
#          cancelled and the flag was permanently stale. FIX: Changed
#          both locations to only set the flag when
#          self.structures(TWILIGHTCOUNCIL) physically exists.
#      (c) TWILIGHT BUILDER HIJACK: The emergency twilight build
#          assigned builder_probe_tag but did NOT set builder_locked.
#          Without builder_locked, the execute_wall_off() code at line
#          46090 could clear the builder state (releasing the probe for
#          mining), and other systems could overwrite the probe's orders.
#          FIX: Set builder_locked = True when assigning the emergency
#          twilight build, and ensure builder_locked is cleared in ALL
#          exit paths of is_builder_busy() for the twilight task
#          (hijack, stuck, idle far, retry exhausted, built successfully).
# 183. STALKER/IMMORTAL KITE STANDARDIZATION — 6 DISTANCE FROM NEAREST ENEMY:
#      The stalker kiting micro was inconsistent across multiple sections:
#      - Some only kited from ZERGLINGS (not roaches, hydras, etc.)
#      - Some used only 3.0 distance instead of 6.0
#      - Some only triggered when enemy was within 5.0 range instead of 6.0
#      The correct behavior: when on weapon cooldown, move to exactly 6 distance
#      from the nearest enemy unit (in the direction away from it). This keeps
#      the stalker at max attack range (6) so it can fire immediately when
#      cooldown expires, while staying out of shorter-range enemies' reach.
#      CHANGES:
#      (a) Wall defense / gw2 defense: Changed threshold from dist < 5.0 to
#          dist <= 6.0 (full attack range). Already used 6 kite distance.
#      (b) Sentry-follow combat, sweep no-sentry, base defense: Changed from
#          zergling-only kiting to kiting from ANY nearest enemy. Removed
#          self.vs_zerg guard (applies to all matchups). Changed < 6.0 to
#          <= 6.0 threshold.
#      (c) Air defense stalker kite: Changed from 3 distance to 6 distance.
#          Also added kite-to-6 on cooldown even when HP >= 80% (previously
#          only kited when low HP, now always kites on cooldown for
#          consistent max-range behavior).
#      (d) Battery retreat kite: Changed from 3.0 to 6.0 kite distance.
#      (e) Fixed SHILEDBATTERY → SHIELDBATTERY typo at air defense section.
#      EXCEPTIONS PRESERVED: Siege tank dive (move TOWARD tank to get inside
#      min range), cyclone approach (move toward to pressure), depot approach
#      (move toward to maintain vision). These are intentional — kiting away
#      from siege tanks keeps stalkers in their kill zone.
# =========================================================================
# 184. CHANGELING ARMY TARGETING REMOVED — WORKER HUNTER ONLY:
#      Changelings were still being targeted as fallback by the army in
#      three places during the attack push:
#      (a) Sentry lead group: elif changelings → target_unit = changelings
#      (b) Individual unit targeting: if not target_enemy → changelings
#      (c) No-sentry group: elif changelings → target_unit = changelings
#      When a changeling walked into our base during an attack push, the
#      sentry would target it and the entire army would run back to chase
#      it. But changelings require a direct ATTACK command on the unit
#      object (they can't be auto-attacked), and the army was effectively
#      just running to the changeling's position without killing it.
#      FIX: Removed all changeling fallback targeting from the army attack
#      push. The manage_changeling_hunter() function handles changelings
#      by assigning a worker to attack them directly. The army should
#      completely ignore changelings — when no real enemies are visible,
#      the army continues toward waypoint/structure targets instead.
#      Also added CHANGELING/CHANGELINGZEALOT to the enemy_units_nearby
#      exclusion filter so changelings don't block waypoint advancement.
# =========================================================================
# 185. STALKER/IMMORTAL OUTRANGE KITING:
#      Previously, stalkers and immortals would always kite on weapon
#      cooldown from any enemy within 6 distance. This was wasteful
#      against enemies with equal or greater range (marauders at 6,
#      hydras with upgrade at 6, siege tanks at 7+), because kiting
#      from them doesn't create a range advantage — it just wastes DPS
#      and creates formation gaps.
#      FIX: Added outrange check before kiting. Stalkers/immortals now
#      only kite on weapon cooldown when their ground_range exceeds the
#      nearest enemy's ground_range. This means:
#      - Stalker (6) vs Zergling (0.1): kite — outranges
#      - Stalker (6) vs Roach (4): kite — outranges
#      - Stalker (6) vs Hydra (5, no upgrade): kite — outranges
#      - Stalker (6) vs Marauder (6): don't kite — equal range
#      - Stalker (6) vs Hydra (6, upgraded): don't kite — equal range
#      - Stalker (6) vs Siege Tank (7): don't kite — outranged
#      Applied to three locations: sentry-follow combat, no-sentry sweep,
#      and base defense kiting.
# =========================================================================
# 186. CORROSIVE BILE DODGE (PVZ):
#      Ravager corrosive bile deals 60 damage in a radius and can
#      devastate clumped army units. The bile effect appears on the
#      ground ~1.8 seconds before impact, giving time to dodge.
#      Added manage_bile_dodge() that:
#      (a) Detects EffectId.RAVAGERCORROSIVEBILECP effects in self.state.effects
#      (b) Finds our combat units within 5 distance of each bile center
#      (c) Moves those units 5 units away from the bile — AWAY from the
#          nearest ravager (so units don't dodge toward the ravager), or
#          toward the nearest base if no ravager is visible
#      Workers and structures are excluded (workers keep mining, structures
#      can't move). Flying units are excluded (bile only hits ground).
#      Only runs in PvZ (ravagers are a Zerg unit). Called from on_step
#      before army micro so bile dodge takes priority.
# 187. PVT BATTLECRUISER DEFENDERS DURING ATTACK TIMING:
#      When a battlecruiser warped in during our attack timing, stalkers
#      were bouncing back and forth between the attack target and the BC.
#      The pre-attack BC defense (air threat hold / prism hold) correctly
#      sends ALL stalkers to kill the BC. But during attack timing, the
#      per-stalker zonal defense code (manage_pvt_stalker_defense) would
#      detect the BC near ourmain/ournat and issue attack commands, while
#      the attack army code would also issue attack-move commands toward
#      the enemy base. Stalkers received conflicting orders every frame,
#      causing them to bounce between the two targets without killing either.
#
#      FIX: Added _pvt_bc_defender_tags system (mirrors banshee/medivac
#      defender pattern). When a BC is within 25 of ourmain or ournat,
#      the 6 closest stalkers are assigned as BC defenders. They are
#      excluded from the main attack army and the stalker defense pool,
#      and each is ordered to attack the BC. The remaining stalkers
#      continue the attack push without bouncing. When no BCs are near
#      our bases, all BC defenders are released back to the main army.
#      The radius is 25 (tighter than banshee's 20 or the pre-attack
#      code's 35) because during attack timing we want to commit most
#      stalkers to the push — only pull back stalkers if the BC is
#      actively threatening our base structures/workers.
#
# 188. PVT PROXY RAX PYLON TIMING & MARINE SPAM CANNON DEFENSE:
#      Two fixes for the proxy barracks rush scenario:
#
#      A. PYLON TIMING FIX: During the proxy rax wall-off build, the builder
#         probe was being pulled away from building the cyber core to build an
#         unnecessary supply pylon. This happened because manage_supply_midgame()
#         used self.build() which can steal the builder probe via SC2's worker
#         selection. The natural nexus (step 4 in the emergency build) provides
#         15 supply when it completes — more than enough to cover us until then.
#         FIX: Extended the proxy_rax guard in manage_supply_midgame() to also
#         block supply pylons when: (a) emergency_wall_active and cyber core not
#         built yet, and (b) when _pvt_proxy_rax is True, until the natural
#         nexus is ready. This ensures the builder probe stays focused on the
#         cyber core and doesn't get hijacked by supply pylon building.
#
#      B. MARINE SPAM CANNON PLACEMENT: When facing a proxy barracks rush with
#         >2 marines within 50 of ourmain before 2:30, the wall-off with just
#         stalkers and a shield battery wasn't enough to hold marine pressure.
#         FIX: Added manage_pvt_marine_spam_cannons() which builds 2 additional
#         cannons inside the wall — one behind each gateway (gw1, gw2).
#         Placement criteria:
#         - Must pass can_place check
#         - Must be inside the wall (not further from nexus than the gateway)
#         - Prioritize position furthest from nexus while edge tiles touch the gw
#         - Prioritize side where closest marine is
#         - As close to terrain/structures as possible
#         Uses a separate free worker (not the builder probe) to avoid
#         disrupting the wall-off build order. The timing condition (before
#         2:30) ensures we only invest in cannons during the critical defense
#         window when marine pressure is highest.
#
# 189. PVZ ROBO PROBE FROM 3RD BASE & HATCH-FIRST GATEWAY TIMING:
#      Two fixes for the PvZ economic opponent scenario:
#
#      A. ROBO PROBE SELECTION: When building a robo inside our main base,
#         get_free_worker(pos) would select the closest free worker, which
#         could be from the 3rd mineral line. That worker can't path through
#         our wall to reach the main base, so the robo order sits stale for
#         40+ seconds before the stale builder timeout retries with a
#         different worker. In the logged game, the first robo attempt at
#         (128.5, 42.5) used a 3rd-base worker that never arrived, and it
#         took 42.6 seconds before the stale builder was replaced.
#         FIX: Added exclude_3rd_base logic to _pvz_try_build_robo(). If
#         the robo position is NOT within 12 of our3rd, exclude 3rd-base
#         workers and only use main/nat miners who can path to the position.
#
#      B. HATCH-FIRST GATEWAY TIMING: In games vs economic opponents where
#         hatch_first_reaction is True but hatch_first_lings_spotted is
#         False (no early lings), manage_flower_production() required a
#         Twilight Council before building gateways in the main base. Since
#         the hatch-first build order puts Forge/Twilight at the END (after
#         Nexus3rd, Core, Gas, Zealot, Gas2, Gate, Sentry, Adepts, Pylon),
#         twilight wasn't built until ~275s. This left the bot sitting at
#         only 2 gateways for over 3 minutes, massively behind on production
#         capacity against a greedy 3-base opponent.
#         FIX: Added an exception for hatch_first_reaction (no lings) in
#         the twilight prerequisite check. When we've correctly scouted a
#         greedy economic opponent with no early pressure, allow flower
#         production to build gateways before twilight exists. We still need
#         pylons first (they provide power), but gateways don't need twilight
#         to be useful — they can produce zealots immediately.
#
# 195. PVT ADEPT/SENTRY BATTERY LEASH:
#      In the reaper_response PvT defense path, the adept and sentry were
#      freely chasing ground threats (marines, etc.) beyond the shield
#      battery's shielding range (7 range). They would run out to meet
#      enemies approaching the base, leaving the battery's protective
#      coverage and dying unnecessarily. Meanwhile, when idle with a
#      shield battery up, they stood at the wallpylon or pre-attack rally
#      instead of moving to the battery leash position (battery+toward
#      map center+5) where they could be shielded while watching for
#      enemies.
#
#      FIX: Added battery-centric leash (7 range) for both adept and
#      sentry, mirroring the PvP stalker defense pattern:
#      - Compute battery position and leash position (battery+toward
#        map_center+5) at the start of the non-stalker defense loop.
#      - If unit is BEYOND 7 range from the battery, attack-move back
#        to the leash position (shoots enemies on the way back).
#      - Sentry: NEVER bypasses the battery leash (too slow/expensive).
#      - Adept: Only bypasses the leash when defending against a reaper
#        within the base area (15 from ournat / 25 from ourmain).
#      - Idle position: Move to leash position when battery is up,
#        instead of wallpylon or pre-attack rally.
#
# 190. PVZ GAS3/GAS4 CANCELLATION & TWILIGHT BUILDER HIJACK:
#      Two fixes for interconnected PvZ issues:
#
#      A. GAS3/GAS4 CANCELLATION: When the 2nd robo triggers 3rd+4th gas,
#         the code used get_free_worker() and worker.build(ASSIMILATOR) but
#         didn't track the builder probe tag. On the next frame,
#         manage_complex_mining() saw the worker as an eligible miner and
#         issued HARVEST_GATHER, cancelling the assimilator build order.
#         The assimilator was ordered and immediately cancelled every frame.
#         FIX: Added _pvz_gas3_probe_tag, _pvz_gas4_probe_tag tracking
#         (plus _pvz_gas3_geyser_tag, _pvz_gas4_geyser_tag). Builder tags
#         are added to away_tags in manage_complex_mining() and excluded
#         from get_free_worker(). Tags are released when the assimilator
#         is complete (checked each frame in manage_pvz_roach_response).
#
#      B. TWILIGHT BUILDER HIJACK: The twilight builder was being stolen
#         by self.build(PYLON) in manage_supply_midgame(). This framework
#         method doesn't respect builder_probe_tag or builder_locked — it
#         just picks the nearest available worker. When the twilight builder
#         was still moving to the position (not yet building),
#         already_pending(TWILIGHTCOUNCIL) returned 0, so the has_twilight
#         guard didn't protect it. self.build() stole the builder each
#         frame, causing a bounce loop: assign → steal → clear → reassign.
#         FIX: (1) Added builder_current_task == "twilight" to the
#         has_twilight check in manage_supply_midgame(), so the guard
#         covers the travel period too. (2) Added builder_locked guard
#         before self.build() calls to prevent stealing any locked builder.
#
# 191. PVZ FORGE_FIRST LOW LING COUNT: SENTRY INSTEAD OF MASS ADEPTS:
#      When we went forge_first (e.g. vs 12-pool) and the Zerg only made
#      a small number of lings (< 10 before 2:45), the wall cannon can
#      handle the defense alone. But manage_second_adept_defense() saw
#      lings near the wall and trained 5 adepts (500 minerals + 125 gas),
#      wasting resources that should have gone toward earlier robo and
#      immortal production. In the logged game, the bot trained 5 adepts
#      for just 2 lings, didn't get a sentry until ~300s, and didn't
#      scout the roach warren until 325s — by which time roaches were
#      already attacking. The immortals came way too late.
#
#      FIX: Added _pvz_forge_first_low_lings flag. When forge_first
#      opening + completed cannon + < 10 enemy zerglings before 2:45,
#      manage_second_adept_defense() skips adept massing and only
#      produces 1 sentry (for hallucination scout + guardian shield).
#      The sentry's hallucination phoenix scouts the roach warren
#      earlier, triggering roach defense path (robo + immortals) on
#      time. The 125 gas saved from not producing 5 adepts funds the
#      earlier robo. The flag is cancelled if ling count spikes to 10+.
#
# 192. PVZ SPIRE RESPONSE: DOUBLE-QUEUE FIX + GAS + STALKER PRODUCTION:
#      Three interconnected bugs when the spire is scouted in PvZ:
#
#      A. DOUBLE-QUEUE: manage_second_adept_defense() trains adepts from
#         idle gateways when lings are near the wall, while manage_army_production()
#         SEQUENCE 4 trains zealots after charge starts. Both run independently
#         on the same frame and can each grab a different gateway, resulting in
#         an adept + zealot produced on the same frame when we should only
#         produce one unit. FIX: Added _army_produced_this_frame flag that is
#         reset each frame in on_step() and set by both functions when they
#         produce. manage_second_adept_defense() checks it before producing.
#         Also, manage_second_adept_defense() now returns immediately when
#         _pvz_spire_seen is True (stalkers only vs mutas, no adepts needed).
#
#      B. NO 3RD/4TH GAS: When spire was detected, the bot stayed on 2 gas
#         and continued the gas transfer (pulling workers off gas after 100
#         for twilight). This left insufficient gas income for stalker mass —
#         the bot produced zealots instead of stalkers because it couldn't
#         afford them. In the logged game, at t=360s with spire active, the
#         bot had 2 gas, 1 stalker, and 14 zealots — entirely useless vs
#         mutalisks. FIX: (1) Added spire check to manage_gas_transfer() —
#         never pull gas workers when spire is seen. (2) Added
#         _pvz_spire_gas_needed flag in _check_spire() that triggers 3rd+4th
#         gas building in pvz_logic(), using the same builder tracking as
#         the roach gas34 code.
#
#      C. ZEALOT PRODUCTION INSTEAD OF STALKERS: After spire was detected,
#         manage_army_production SEQUENCE 4 continued producing zealots
#         (because _produce_zealots_general was True for PvZ without roach
#         warren). Zealots can't attack air — they're useless vs mutalisks.
#         FIX: Added _pvz_spire_mode flag. When spire is seen, SEQUENCE 4
#         produces stalkers (gas >= 50) or zealots as mineral dump (gas < 50),
#         similar to the _pvz_roach_mode branch. This ensures we mass
#         stalkers for anti-air while still spending minerals when gas is low.
# =========================================================================

# 193. PVT FORGE_FIRST (PROXY RAX) DEFENSE + GATEWAY + PYLON FIXES:
#      Multiple issues in the PvT forge-first response path:
#
#      A. STALKERS RUNNING TO ENEMY BASE: The proxy_rax path started a map
#         sweep immediately when the first stalker spawned, sending stalkers
#         toward the enemy supply depot wall. Units should defend at the wall
#         pylon inside our base until the tech timing attack triggers (charge
#         + armor). For forge_first, wall_rally = wallpylon (not battery+5
#         toward map center, which is outside the wall).
#         FIX: Disabled map sweep for forge_first/proxy_rax path. Stalkers
#         rally at wallpylon when no enemies are attacking, and only push
#         out when attack_time_target triggers after charge+armor.
#         The 2:20 no-reaper auto-commit is also disabled for proxy_rax.
#
#      B. GATEWAY LIMIT STUCK AT 4: manage_flower_production() hardcoded
#         gateway_limit=4 for proxy_rax, preventing the chargelot +1 armor
#         7-gateway warpgate build from ever building gates 5-7. The opponent
#         expanded instead of attacking and the bot never transitioned.
#         FIX: gateway_limit now transitions from 4 to 7 once warpgate
#         research has started AND +1 armor has been started, since these
#         mark the transition from defense to timing attack preparation.
#
#      C. PYLON PRODUCTION STALLING: manage_supply_midgame() blocked all
#         pylon production for proxy_rax until the natural nexus was ready.
#         When the nat nexus was delayed, the bot became supply-blocked
#         and couldn't produce gateway units or workers.
#         FIX: Allow pylon production when supply-blocked (supply_left < 6)
#         even before nat nexus is ready, but cap at 2 total pylons
#         (wallpylon + 1 main pylon). No extra pylons until nat nexus.
#
#      D. MINERAL BANKING WHILE WAITING FOR TWILIGHT: When gas was being
#         saved for the twilight council (125 min / 50 gas), the bot banked
#         450+ minerals because the existing 2 gateways were in production.
#         FIX: Added mineral buffer logic in forge_first production — when
#         minerals > 275 (150 for gateway + 125 reserved for twilight) and
#         twilight hasn't been built yet, build additional gateways up to
#         the 7-gateway cap. This ensures gateways are ready when charge
#         completes, enabling immediate chargelot warp-in waves.
# =========================================================================

# 194. PVT CC-FIRST PIVOT GATEWAY BUILD + BUILDER LOCK BOUNCE FIX:
#      Two issues in the PvT CC-first → gateway-first pivot path:
#
#      A. GATEWAY ORDERED BUT NOT STARTED BEFORE NEXUS: When the CC-first
#         pivot detected gas and redirected the probe to build gateway first
#         (state 1.5), the state machine immediately transitioned to state 1
#         (nexus next) after calling probe.build(). But probe.build() just
#         queues the build order — the probe still needs to walk to gw1 and
#         start construction. State 1 then detected the gateway as "pending"
#         and cleared the builder task, redirecting the probe to the nexus
#         position before the gateway was actually placed on the map. The
#         gw_first state machine had to recover and rebuild the gateway ~7s
#         later.
#         FIX: State 1.5 no longer transitions after probe.build(). It stays
#         in state 1.5 until the gateway structure physically appears on the
#         map (gw_exists_15 check). The gw_pending_15 pre-move also only
#         runs after the gateway has started (gw_exists_15), preventing the
#         probe from walking away before the build command executes. State 1's
#         stale gateway task clear also only triggers when the gateway EXISTS
#         (not just pending).
#
#      B. BUILDER LOCK CLEARED EVERY FRAME: The reaper response state machine
#         cleared builder_locked and builder_current_task every frame when
#         state >= 10 (research phase). This fought with manage_flower_production()
#         which set builder_locked=True and assigned pylon tasks. Each frame:
#           1. Flower production assigns pylon task, sets builder_locked=True
#           2. Reaper state machine clears builder_locked and builder_current_task
#           3. Mining system claims the "free" builder, pulling it away
#           4. Next frame, cycle repeats — probe bounces between pylon and
#              gateway positions indefinitely, never building either
#         The pylon only got built when charge finished because warpgates
#         went briefly idle after warping units, changing the gateway build
#         condition and breaking the cycle.
#         FIX: Only clear builder_locked ONCE when state first reaches >= 10,
#         using _pvt_reaper_builder_released flag. After the initial release,
#         flower production owns the builder and its lock/task are preserved
#         across frames.
# 198. PYLON BUILD LOCK: RELEASE BUILDER WHEN PYLON IS PLANTED (NOT COMPLETED):
#      The pylon build lock (_flower_pylon_ordered) and is_builder_busy() both
#      held the builder probe locked until the pylon was READY (fully completed,
#      ~18 seconds of construction). This serialized pylon construction: the
#      builder walked to a position, planted the pylon, then stood idle for 18s
#      waiting for it to finish, then walked to the next position. Result: only
#      1 pylon per 25+ seconds. SC2 buildings construct themselves after build()
#      is issued — the probe does NOT need to stay. The fix releases the builder
#      as soon as the pylon appears on the map (build_progress > 0), allowing
#      continuous construction: walk → plant → walk → plant. The old race
#      condition (DEV NOTE #177: pylon appears → builder freed → new position
#      cancels current build) is prevented by the _flower_pylon_ordered lock,
#      which blocks new position searches until the current pylon is planted.
# 199. ZEALOT STRUCTURE TARGETING: ATTACK-MOVE TO POSITION, NOT DIRECT ATTACK:
#      When zealots (and other melee units like adepts) targeted enemy structures
#      with unit.attack(structure), they would walk directly to the structure,
#      ignoring enemy units along the way. This caused zealots to attack a CC
#      while a bio ball of marines/marauders stood right next to them, shooting
#      freely. The fix: melee units now use unit.attack(structure.position) when
#      targeting structures, which issues an attack-move to that position. Attack-
#      move causes the zealot to engage any enemy units it encounters en route,
#      only attacking the structure once all nearby enemy units are dead. Ranged
#      units (stalkers, immortals) still use direct attack(structure) since they
#      shoot from range and don't need to path through enemies.
# 200. BUILDER PROBES MUST BE EXCLUDED FROM MINING VIA away_tags:
#      UNIVERSAL RULE: ANY probe that is assigned to build a structure MUST have
#      its tag tracked in a dedicated variable and added to the away_tags set
#      in manage_complex_mining(). Without this, the mining system sees the
#      probe as eligible for mining and issues HARVEST_GATHER/RETURN orders
#      every frame, overriding the build command. The probe bounces between
#      the build position and the mineral line indefinitely — the structure
#      is never built.
#
#      This happened in PvP DT defense (_pvp_dt_defense_build, states 20-24):
#      each state called get_free_worker() + probe.build() but never tracked
#      the probe tag. The mining system reassigned the probe every frame.
#      Result: forge never built, 1,890+ failed build commands over 235 seconds.
#
#      FIX: Added _pvp_dt_builder_tag to track the DT defense builder probe.
#      Each build state reuses the tracked probe (or finds a new one) and
#      stores its tag. The tag is added to away_tags so mining excludes it.
#      The tag is cleared when the building appears or when the state completes.
#
#      PRINCIPLE: Every get_free_worker() + probe.build() call site MUST:
#        1. Track the probe tag in a dedicated variable (e.g. _xyz_builder_tag)
#        2. Add that variable to the away_tags set in manage_complex_mining()
#        3. Clear the tag when the building appears (or the task completes)
#        4. Reuse the tracked probe on subsequent frames instead of calling
#           get_free_worker() again (which returns a different probe each frame)
# 201. CHARGELOT BILE EXCLUSION — PUSH FORWARD INSTEAD OF RETREAT:
#      When ravager corrosive bile lands near our army, the bile dodge code
#      (DEV NOTE #186) moves all combat units away. This causes zealots to
#      bounce between retreat (bile dodge MOVE) and attack (army micro ATTACK)
#      commands every frame, so they never actually deal damage.
#
#      FIX: Zealots are excluded from the bile retreat. Instead, when a bile
#      is nearby and a zealot is on weapon cooldown, the zealot moves TOWARD
#      the nearest enemy unit (push forward). When off cooldown and near a
#      bile, the zealot attacks the nearest enemy. This only applies after
#      the Charge upgrade is complete (chargelots). Pre-charge zealots are
#      also excluded from bile retreat — they don't get the push-forward
#      logic but also don't jitter, since army micro handles them normally
#      without the bile dodge interference.
#
#      Rationale: Chargelots are melee — retreating from bile means giving up
#      ground and getting kited. A 60-damage bile hit is far less costly than
#      losing all zealot DPS to command jitter. Pushing forward keeps
#      chargelots in the fight and forces the enemy to deal with them.
# 202. PVP FORGE_FIRST → VOIDRAY TRANSITION: TWO BUGS BLOCKING ATTACK TIMING:
#      After cannon rush / forge_first defense, the bot transitions to a
#      voidray build. But the attack timing NEVER triggered, leaving the bot
#      in permanent defense mode with 30+ stalkers and 0 attack push.
#
#      BUG A: Air upgrade research required 2+ stargates all busy producing.
#      During 1-base all-in, stargates are capped at 1, so the air upgrade
#      flag (_pvp_air_armor_started) was never set. Without air upgrades,
#      the attack timing condition (air upgrade done + 3 voidrays) was
#      permanently false. FIX: Accept 1 stargate that is busy (not idle) as
#      sufficient to start air upgrades during 1-base all-in.
#
#      BUG B: 1-base all-in emergency shield battery builder probe bounced
#      between move position and mining. The builder.move(build_pos) call
#      did not set builder_current_task or builder_task_target, so
#      is_builder_busy() did not protect the probe. Other systems (flower
#      production, voidray build) stole the probe every frame, issuing
#      competing commands. FIX: Set builder_current_task = "1base_battery"
#      and builder_task_target when the builder is walking to or waiting at
#      the battery position. Clear the task when the battery is complete or
#      the position is skipped.
# 203. PVT ARMY WIPE RETREAT INFINITE LOOP (move-out timer never fires):
#      When the first attack wave dies and the army retreats for 60s, the
#      "original army wiped" check (comparing stale snapshot tags against
#      live units) would re-trigger EVERY TIME the retreat timer expired,
#      because the old snapshot still contained 0 alive units. This reset
#      the timer to +60s indefinitely, trapping the army in permanent retreat.
#
#      ROOT CAUSE: The wipe check condition was `_pvt_army_wipe_retreat_until <= self.time`
#      which is TRUE both before any retreat (timer=0) AND after the timer expires.
#      The recovery code (take new snapshot, resume attack) was structurally
#      unreachable because the wipe check ran first and reset the timer.
#
#      FIX: Two changes:
#      1. Guard the wipe check with `_pvt_army_wipe_retreat_until == 0` (only
#         run when NOT in a retreat, not just when the timer has expired).
#      2. Reset `_pvt_army_wipe_retreat_until = 0` in the recovery section so
#         the guard allows the next wipe detection cycle.
#
#  204. PVT FORGE_FIRST WARPGATE PRODUCTION STALL (no warp-ins after morph):
#      After gateways morphed to warpgates, ALL unit production stopped permanently.
#      The army stayed at 4 stalkers + 4 zealots with 7 idle warpgates for the
#      entire game. Two root causes:
#
#      BUG A: The forge_first "After charge" zealot production code used
#      find_placement() with a fallback to gw.warp_in() at the PYLON'S OWN
#      POSITION. The pylon position is occupied by the pylon building, so the
#      game silently rejects the warp-in command. No error is raised, no unit
#      is produced, and the warpgate stays "idle" forever. Every frame repeats
#      the same failed warp-in, creating a permanent production halt.
#
#      BUG B: The forge_first "Before charge" Step 2 (sentry production) used
#      gw.train() which doesn't work on warpgates. After the first 2 stalkers
#      were produced (on regular gateways before morph), Step 2 would try
#      gw.train(SENTRY) on a warpgate — silently fails — then returns,
#      blocking all subsequent production Steps.
#
#      FIX: Added _forge_first_warp_in() helper that uses the same robust
#      approach as SEQUENCE 4: random offsets + can_place() first, then
#      find_placement() fallback, and NEVER warps directly at the pylon
#      position. Replaced all gw.train() calls on warpgates with this helper.
#
#  205. PVZ OBSERVER TIMING DELAY WHEN CANNON EXISTS (forge first):
#      When going forge first vs roach warren, the observer was built as
#      Priority 1 from the robo, delaying immortal production. But when we
#      have a cannon already (forge first → cannon), the cannon provides
#      detection for base defense against burrowed roaches. Building an
#      observer first delays our immortal timing attack by ~30 seconds.
#
#      FIX: When a cannon exists, delay the observer until 1 immortal before
#      the attack trigger count. If attack triggers at 2 immortals (1-base
#      roach): build 1 immortal → observer → 1 immortal. If attack triggers
#      at 4 immortals (multi-base roach): build 3 immortals → observer →
#      1 immortal. Without a cannon, observer is still Priority 1 (no
#      detection = vulnerable to burrowed roaches).
#
#  206. PVZ MAP SWEEP CIRCLING BETWEEN ENEMYNAT AND ENEMEMYMAIN:
#      After the immortal push triggered, the army would reach enemynat,
#      clear it, advance to enemymain, then bounce BACK to enemynat instead
#      of continuing the sweep. This happened because the no-sentry sweep
#      advance condition (line ~22062) required BOTH: no enemies AND no
#      structures within radius AND army within 5 of waypoint AND no known
#      structures on the ENTIRE map. The last condition was nearly always
#      false (Zerg always has creep tumors/spores somewhere), so the sweep
#      index never advanced past enemymain. The army would then get new
#      attack orders to target the closest known structure, which was often
#      back at enemynat (rebuilt or leftover), creating an infinite circle.
#
#      FIX: Added PvZ-specific vision-based sweep advance: when we have
#      vision at the current waypoint AND no visible enemies/structures
#      within 15 range, advance to the next waypoint. This mirrors the
#      PvT reaper_response vision advance logic (DEV NOTE #159) and
#      prevents the army from bouncing between cleared bases. Also
#      added similar vision advance for the sentry path in PvZ.
# =========================================================================
#  207. PVT HALLUC PHOENIX SCOUT KILLED BY CYCLONE (no avoidance):
#      The hallucinated phoenix scout had no cyclone avoidance logic. It would
#      beeline toward enemymain/enemynat and fly straight over an enemy cyclone,
#      which locks on and kills the hallucination instantly. The phoenix only
#      had marine wrap avoidance (3+ marines near enemymain), but no unit-level
#      threat detection. Cyclones are particularly dangerous to hallucinations
#      because lock-on range is ~7, damage is very high, and the halluc has
#      very low HP.
#
#      FIX: Added STATE 0 (cyclone avoidance) as the highest-priority state in
#      manage_pvt_halluc_scout(). When a cyclone is within 10 distance of the
#      phoenix, the code generates a wide half-circle wrap around the cyclone
#      (radius=max(12, dist+3), ~55% of a circle). The wrap direction (CW or
#      CCW) is chosen using the cross product of (cyclone→phoenix) and
#      (cyclone→resume_target), so the phoenix wraps around the side of the
#      cyclone that's closest to its intended path. After the avoidance arc
#      completes, the phoenix resumes its original destination.
#      State variables: _phoenix_cyclone_avoiding, _phoenix_cyclone_waypoints,
#      _phoenix_cyclone_wp_index, _phoenix_cyclone_resume_target,
#      _phoenix_cyclone_tag. These reset when a new hallucination is cast.
# =========================================================================
#  208. STALKER ATTACK-MOVE JITTER: ATTACK OVERRIDDEN BY MOVE EVERY FRAME:
#      During the PvT attack sweep, stalkers were issued ATTACK(enemy) by
#      the sweep targeting code, then immediately overridden by MOVE(sentry)
#      or MOVE(observer) from the "no threats near sentry" fallback branch.
#      This happened every other frame: ATTACK→MOVE→ATTACK→MOVE, causing
#      2000+ attack resets and 0 attacks landed across an entire game.
#
#      ROOT CAUSE: In manage_army_movement's sweep section and in
#      _pvt_sweep_attack_units, when no enemies were within 15 of the sentry
#      AND the unit was already attacking (is_attacking=True), the code
#      checked if enemies were in the unit's IMMEDIATE range (7 distance).
#      If the enemy was 8-10 away (stalker walking toward it to get in range),
#      the guard failed and MOVE(sentry) or MOVE(observer) was issued,
#      cancelling the ATTACK. Next frame, the sweep code re-issued ATTACK,
#      then MOVE overrode again, ad infinitum.
#
#      FIX: Added guard in THREE locations: (1) manage_army_movement sweep
#      obs2_too_far branch, (2) manage_army_movement sweep is_attacking
#      branch (move to sentry), (3) _pvt_sweep_attack_units obs2_too_far
#      branch, (4) _pvt_sweep_attack_units is_attacking branch (move to
#      sentry). Each guard checks if the unit's current ATTACK order targets
#      a real enemy unit (by tag lookup via enemy_units.find_by_tag). If the
#      target is a living enemy unit, the ATTACK is preserved — don't
#      override with MOVE. The stalker is closing distance to get in range,
#      which is a valid state that shouldn't be interrupted.
#  209. PVZ ROACH RUSH IMMORTAL PRIORITY + BILE BOUNCE:
#      Two issues found in a PvZ game where roaches rushed our base:
#
#      (a) OBSERVER BEFORE IMMORTALS WHEN UNDER ATTACK: When roaches were
#      actively attacking near our bases (within 30 of main/nat/3rd), the
#      robo still produced an observer first (Priority 1), delaying the
#      first immortal by 30+ seconds. Against a roach rush, immortals
#      are critical — they deal 40 bonus damage vs armored roaches.
#      An observer provides detection but zero combat value. We saw the
#      roaches coming but couldn't produce the units we needed to fight
#      them because the observer was in the way.
#
#      FIX: Extended the observer delay logic (previously only for cannon/
#      forge-first) to also trigger when enemy roaches are near our bases.
#      When _roaches_near_base is True (enemy roaches within 30 of any
#      of our bases), the observer is delayed until (attack_trigger - 1)
#      immortals are built, same as the cannon delay. This gives us the
#      anti-armor damage we need to survive the push. The observer is
#      still built before the final immortal so we have detection for
#      burrowed roaches by the time we push out.
#
#      (b) BILE DODGE CAUSING ATTACK-MOVE BOUNCE: When ravagers used
#      corrosive bile near our army, manage_bile_dodge() issued MOVE
#      commands to retreat units from the bile. But the army micro code
#      then issued ATTACK commands, and next frame the bile dodge issued
#      MOVE again. This created an endless ATTACK→MOVE→ATTACK→MOVE
#      bounce every 2 frames. In the log, stalkers had 644+ attack
#      resets in ~10 seconds — they jittered in place and never fired.
#      The 60-damage bile hit is far less costly than zero DPS from
#      endless jittering.
#
#      FIX: Removed the bile retreat movement entirely. Instead, when
#      bile is incoming, ALL combat units (stalkers, immortals, sentries,
#      zealots) push FORWARD toward the nearest enemy unit. This extends
#      the chargelot push-forward (DEV NOTE #201) to all unit types.
#      On weapon cooldown + bile nearby: move toward nearest enemy.
#      Off cooldown + bile nearby: attack nearest enemy. No retreat
#      movement is issued at all. The unified push-forward avoids the
#      MOVE/ATTACK conflict that caused the jitter.
#
#  210. PVP DT SHRINE DETECTED BUT FORGE/CANNONS NEVER BUILT:
#      When a Dark Shrine or Templar Archive was scouted, the detection
#      code correctly set _pvp_dt_detected = True, but the forge/cannon
#      build chain never ran because _pvp_dt_defense_build() was only
#      called inside the pvp_voidray block of pvp_logic(). If the opening
#      was nexus_first, gateway_first, or forge_first, the DT defense
#      function was never called at all. Even for pvp_voidray, the
#      function had a redundant guard `opening_build_chosen != "pvp_voidray"`
#      that would have blocked it if called from another path.
#
#      FIX: (a) Moved _pvp_dt_defense_build() call to run unconditionally
#      for ALL PvP openings (after the if/elif blocks in pvp_logic).
#      (b) Removed the pvp_voidray-only guard inside _pvp_dt_defense_build().
#      (c) Added _pvp_dt_builder_tag to get_free_worker exclusion list so
#      other systems don't steal the DT defense builder probe.
#
#  DEV NOTE #211: find_by_tag() returns None if the unit is dead/gone.
#      Do NOT call .is_alive or .is_active on the result — just check
#      truthiness. Both .is_alive and .is_active raise AttributeError
#      on Unit objects in python-sc2. The correct pattern is:
#        unit = self.enemy_units.find_by_tag(tag)
#        if unit:  # None means dead/gone, any Unit object means alive
#            ...
#
#  211. PVT LOCK-ON FLEE + ADEPT LOCK-ON FLEE (DEV NOTE #138):
#      (a) STALKER LOCK-ON FLEE: The existing anti-cyclone micro (has_buff
#      BuffId.LOCKON → flee -10 range) correctly makes locked-on stalkers
#      flee. Non-locked stalkers should still approach and attack cyclones
#      — with 2+ stalkers, the locked one flees while the other continues
#      attacking. With 1 stalker, it can chase/approach the cyclone and
#      if it gets locked on, it flees to disengage. The key fix is ensuring
#      LOCKON flee actually runs and isn't overridden: the _cyclone_flee_tags
#      set prevents defense micro from overriding flee orders with attack
#      orders, breaking the bounce loop.
#      (b) ADEPT LOCK-ON FLEE: The adept had NO LOCKON buff check in its
#      cyclone defense code. It would kite on cooldown if the cyclone was
#      within 8 range, but if it got locked on, it would stop kiting and
#      try to attack/hold position instead of fleeing. A locked-on adept
#      is a dead adept — it's slower than stalkers and can't blink.
#      FIX: Added has_buff(BuffId.LOCKON) check as the FIRST thing in the
#      adept cyclone defense section. If the adept is locked on, it flees
#      -10 range from the cyclone and continues to the next adept.
#      This mirrors the stalker LOCKON flee logic.
# =========================================================================
#  DEV NOTE #212: 4-GATE PATH SKIPS AIR PIVOT. The 4-GATE all-in path
#      in on_step() has a `return` that skips the NORMAL OPERATION section,
