# =========================================================================
#  214. PVT DUPLICATE ADEPT/SENTRY FROM FLAG MISMATCH (DEV NOTE #213):
#      The FOURG state machine trains adept+sentry via
#      _pvt_proxy_hidden_tech_next_unit(), which tracks them with
#      _pvt_proxy_hidden_tech_adept_done / _pvt_proxy_hidden_tech_sentry_done.
#      But the parallel training code in execute_pvt_reaper_response() uses
#      DIFFERENT flags: _pvt_adept_trained / _pvt_sentry_trained.
#      The FOURG path never set the parallel flags, so the parallel code
#      trained a DUPLICATE adept (t=295s, 75 min + 25 gas) and duplicate
#      sentry (t=358s, 50 min + 100 gas) even though the FOURG path already
#      produced them at t=127s and t=154s. This wasted 125 min + 125 gas and
#      blocked stalker production for ~60s (the parallel code waits to afford
#      the duplicate sentry at 100 gas before moving to stalkers), causing
#      gateways to sit idle and minerals to pile up to 2000+.
#      FIX: At the top of the parallel training block (state >= 5 and < 13),
#      sync the proxy hidden tech flags to the parallel training flags:
#      if _pvt_proxy_hidden_tech_adept_done is True, set _pvt_adept_trained = True
#      if _pvt_proxy_hidden_tech_sentry_done is True, set _pvt_sentry_trained = True
#      This ensures the parallel code skips adept/sentry and goes straight to
#      stalkers when the FOURG path already produced them.
# =========================================================================
#  215. PVT EARLY FLOWER TRANSITION (reaper_response state machine):
#      PROBLEM: The reaper_response state machine keeps the builder probe
#      locked through states 5-9 (pylon → gw2 → battery → forge → twilight),
#      building them sequentially one at a time. By the time 2 stalkers are
#      out (~t=150-180s), the bot has banked 800+ minerals that
#      manage_flower_production can't spend because the builder is locked.
#      Money piles up during 3:15-5min while the state machine slowly
#      advances through its sequential build chain.
#      FIX: After 2 stalkers are out (state in [5,10]), force the state
#      machine to jump to state 10. State 10:
#        - Releases the builder probe (one-shot via _pvt_reaper_builder_released)
#        - Handles research (armor if forge exists, charge if twilight exists)
#        - Advances to state 12 (warpgate) then 13 (done)
#      Meanwhile, manage_flower_production uses the freed probe to build
#      pylons and gateways in parallel with the research phase. This solves
#      the "money not being used" issue.
#      GUARDS:
#        - Skipped for proxy_marauder (different build path)
#        - state >= 5: parallel training has had a chance to produce stalkers
#        - state < 10: not already in the research/release phase
#        - 2+ stalkers out (alive + pending): enough defense to release builder
#      FOLLOWUP FIXES (so the early transition doesn't break the build):
#        - DEV NOTE #215b: manage_flower_production now builds forge for PvT
#          when the reaper state machine was short-circuited before state 8
#          could build it. Without this, PvT games that transitioned early
#          would never get a forge and never research +1 armor.
#        - DEV NOTE #215c: manage_production_buildings now has a PvT armor
#          research fallback. When state 10 was skipped/short-circuited and
#          a forge is later built by flower production, this fallback starts
#          +1 ground armor research. Also clears _pvt_forge_skipped flag
#          so the attack timing code stops skipping the armor gate.
# =========================================================================
#  216. PVT LOCKON RETREAT TO BATTERY (independent of cyclone vision):
#      PROBLEM: The cyclone LOCKON flee only ran inside the
#      `for cyclone in cyclones:` loop, which was gated on
#      `cyclones = self.enemy_units(UnitTypeId.CYCLONE)`. If the cyclone
#      was on high ground (behind a cliff), in fog of war, or had moved
#      back after locking on, `cyclones` was EMPTY and the LOCKON flee
#      never ran — even though the stalker had the LOCKON buff and was
#      taking damage. Wall defense then issued ATTACK orders every frame,
#      and the stalker bounced between ATTACK and MOVE (from battery
#      retreat or other micro) until it died to lock-on damage
#      (80→15 HP over 3 seconds).
#      FIX: Added a LOCKON buff check that runs BEFORE the cyclone vision
#      loop, for ALL three unit types (stalker, adept, sentry). When a
#      unit has the LOCKON buff, it retreats to the nearest shield battery
#      to stay alive (the battery recharges shields while the unit waits
#      out the lock-on duration). If no battery exists, the unit flees
#      toward ourmain. The unit is added to _cyclone_flee_tags so wall
#      defense / sweep micro skips it entirely (no ATTACK orders that
#      would override the retreat). The existing cyclone-vision loop now
#      also skips stalkers already in _cyclone_flee_tags.
#      User request: "when we got locked onto we tried to run away but
#      then got commanded back to attack the cyclone. We need to be only
#      retreating to the shield battery to stay alive."
#
