#          UnitTypeId.WARPGATE. In PvP, enemies research warpgate early and
#          all their gateways morph to warpgates within ~140s. Our scout
#          saw the warpgates but the flag _pvp_enemy_gateway_seen stayed
#          False forever — we never realized the enemy had gateway tech.
#      (b) detect_enemy_forge() classifies "forge seen before any gateway
#          seen" as a cannon rush: `_is_cannon_rush = not _pvp_enemy_gateway_seen`.
#          Because (a) never set the gateway flag, ANY enemy forge spotted
#          after ~140s would be misclassified as a cannon rush — even when
#          the forge is at the enemy's main base (dist_to_ourmain=123) and
#          the attack push is already underway.
#      (c) When cannon rush was (falsely) detected, the opening was
#          overridden to forge_first, _emergency_4gate_active was set True,
#          and the 4-gate wall-clearing logic (line ~57924) kicked in. That
#          code finds OUR OWN photon cannon at cannon1_pos (a leftover from
#          the earlier actual cannon rush defense at t=51s) and commands
#          ALL army units to attack it. The army walked back across the
#          map to kill our own building.
#      FIX: Three layers of defense (in order of root cause → safety net):
#      (1) detect_enemy_gateway() now also checks for UnitTypeId.WARPGATE,
#          not just GATEWAY. This prevents the false negative that caused
#          the false positive in the first place.
#      (2) detect_enemy_forge() now refuses to classify as cannon rush if
#          ANY of these are true:
#            - Attack push already triggered (_pvp_attack_triggered)
#            - Game time > 240s (4 minutes) — cannon rushes are committed
#              long before this; late forge sightings are tech structures
#            - Enemy has 2+ townhalls (they expanded — not a cannon rush)
#          These guards ensure that even if (1) somehow fails, we don't
#          reset our entire strategy mid-attack.
#      (3) The 4-gate wall-clearing code now skips entirely when
#          _pvp_attack_triggered is True. Even if cannon rush was
#          correctly detected mid-game, the army should NOT abandon the
#          attack push to kill our own wall — the wall can be dealt with
#          later, but throwing away a committed attack is unrecoverable.
#      User request: "In this game when we attacked our zealots and
#      stalkers returned back to base to kill the cannon when they were
#      already out in the enemy base fighting"
