#  229. ARMY MICRO: PILE-ON + MOVE OVERRIDE + STRUCTURE DIVING (PvZ + PvT):
#      PROBLEM: Three compounding micro bugs causing massive DPS loss:
#      (a) PILE-ON: Defense/sweep code calls threats.closest_to(unit) then
#          unit.attack(closest_threat). When there's one enemy in vision,
#          closest_to returns the SAME enemy for every stalker. All stalkers
#          get attack(same_target) — focus-firing one zergling while 20
#          hydras shoot them. Visible in amove.log at t=307.4s: three
#          stalkers within 4 units of each other all got target=4398776321.
#      (b) MOVE OVERRIDE: 2 frames after defense code issues attack(threat),
#          positioning code issues move(rally_point). The attack gets
#          cancelled (stalker walks away from the enemy it was about to
#          shoot). Visible in amoveagain.log: 4,464 "ATTACK RESET!
#          was:ATTACK now:AbilityId.MOVE" entries in ONE PvT game. Root
#          cause: _pvz_defense_order_tags only tracks SAME-FRAME orders;
#          the positioning code runs later in the same frame but the
#          unit.orders check reflects the PREVIOUS frame.
#      (c) STRUCTURE DIVING (PvT march): During the march to the enemy
#          base, stalkers would dive on distant depots/refineries they
#          passed, then bounce between the structure and the siege tank
#          shooting them. The "structs_near_sentry" branch targeted any
#          structure within 15 of the sentry — even structures 30+ units
#          away from the stalker itself.
#      FIX: Three coordinated changes:
#      (1) ATTACK-MOVE TO POSITION (not direct attack on unit). Replace
#          unit.attack(target_enemy) with unit.attack(target_enemy.position)
#          in: PvZ base defense, PvZ zonal defense (air + ground), PvT
#          sweep (sentry + no-sentry paths). attack-MOVE lets SC2
#          auto-acquire the closest enemy for each stalker (no pile-on),
#          doesn't get overridden when the original target dies/enters
#          fog (no MOVE override), and engages enemies along the path
#          ("kill and move on" behavior). EXCEPTION: changelings must be
#          targeted directly (they slip away if not locked).
#      (2) ATTACK-LOCK. New state vars (_attack_lock_tags dict +
#          ATTACK_LOCK_FRAMES=8). Helper methods _record_attack_issued()
#          and _is_attack_locked(). Every unit.attack(...) call in
#          defense/sweep code now records the frame. Positioning code
#          checks _is_attack_locked() before issuing any MOVE command.
#          If the unit was issued an ATTACK in the last 8 frames
#          (~0.35s at 22.4 fps), MOVE is suppressed. This is the safety
#          net that catches orders from previous frames that
#          _pvz_defense_order_tags misses.
#      (3) IGNORE DISTANT STRUCTURES DURING MARCH. While
#          _pvt_main_destroyed is False (enemy main still intact), the
#          sweep code only targets structures within 10 of the unit
#          itself — NOT structures near the sentry. This stops the
#          "bounce between siege tank and depot" behavior. Once the
#          enemy main is destroyed (mopup phase), structures near the
#          sentry are fair game again.
#      User request: "We follow the sentry, if enemies are near the
#      sentry we attack them. We ignore all structures during our march
#      to the enemy base while the enemy main is still intact so we
#      don't ever get to attack any of their structures until we are
#      close to them. Which means our code to follow the sentry means
#      that while an enemy unit is near the sentry we can attack the
#      position of it. Our zealots and stalkers should kill it and move
#      on then."
#
